/* 横向卡 · 第二科（Protein Engineering & Synthetic Biology）第三张
   把一个基因装进载体 —— 每一种克隆方法，以及怎么选。
   出处不是捷克生化书，是她自己的课堂笔记 pesbexplain/data/ch1.js（第 1–2 讲，32 个节点）。
   本卡用到其中二十个：1-3 为什么非走 DNA · 1-4-1 DNA 从哪来 · 1-4-2 RT-PCR 与内含子 ·
   1-4-3 基因合成与密码子优化 · 1-5-3 核酸酶 · 1-5-4 连接酶磷酸酶激酶 · 1-8 设计软件 ·
   1-9 质粒与复制起点 · 1-10-1 抗生素选择与卫星菌落 · 1-10-2 ccdB 负选择 ·
   1-11 限制酶与 IIP/IIS · 1-12 经典酶切克隆 · 1-13 蓝白斑 · 1-14 Golden Gate ·
   1-15 Gateway · 1-16 TA 与 TOPO TA · 1-17 LIC · 1-18 Gibson ·
   1-19 该用哪一套 · 1-20 pSecTag2 那道练习。
   那个文件自己区分两层：points = 幻灯片上有的；beyondPoints = 笔记标明「课上没讲」的延伸。
   卡上凡是来自 beyondPoints 或通用知识的，都当场标了「在 beyondPoints」或「通用」。
   页码用 <span class="pg"> 标的是讲次和幻灯片号，例如 L2 s.20–21。
   接卡 14（转化与电穿孔）、x-rxn（连接酶和核酸酶属于哪类反应）、taq（聚合酶与校对）、
   12（lac 操纵子，所以蓝白斑到底在读什么）、pe-expr（质粒进去之后）、
   03 和 x-bonds（连接酶做的那个磷酸二酯键）。 */

window.CARDS.push({
id:'pe-clone', cross:1, w:0,
q:'把一个基因装进载体 —— 每一种克隆方法，以及怎么选',
qcn:'横向卡 · 第二科第三张 · 所有方法都在回答同一个问题：怎么让两段 DNA 的末端互相找得到',
sub:'跨题共用 · 出处是她自己的 PESB 课堂笔记第 1–2 讲 · 接卡 14、x-rxn、taq、12、pe-expr、03、x-bonds',

cram:[
 {g:'开口 · 先摆骨架，别摆清单', gn:'这一科的第三张卡。<b>七种方法一口气报出来就是一份目录</b>，而笔记最后一节自己说：答案是一个<b>选择</b>。所以先给那条能把所有方法安放进去的轴。'},
 {n:'01', t:'为什么整件事非在 DNA 上做不可',
  big:'产物是蛋白，改动却<b>只能</b>在 DNA 这一层做。完整答案是<b>三层</b>，而大多数人只说第一层',
  en:'“The product is a protein, so why use recombinant DNA technology at all? The answer has three layers. First the central dogma. Information can pass from nucleic acid to nucleic acid and from nucleic acid to protein, but never from protein to protein or from protein to nucleic acid. So a protein cannot be templated and cannot be amplified. There is no protein polymerase and no protein PCR. Second, and this is the layer people leave out, there is a marked absence of tools for targeted manipulation at the protein level. Third, therefore the only way to make a specific change reproducibly and at scale is to make it in the DNA.”',
  note:'<b>“a marked absence of tools for targeted manipulation at the protein level” 是幻灯片的原话</b>，照用。<b>第二层才是考官在等的。</b><span class="pg">L1 s.21</span><br>为什么第一层不够：中心法则只解释了「造不多」，没解释「改不准」。完全可以想象一个世界，蛋白扩增不了，但有一把镊子能精准换掉第 222 位的残基——<b>第二层说的就是这把镊子不存在</b>。<br>⚠ 化学法和酶法确实存在，但都不是反例：<b>NHS 酯</b>认赖氨酸氨基，一个蛋白表面有几十个赖氨酸，你得到的是一锅混合物；<b>马来酰亚胺</b>认半胱氨酸巯基，定点性好得多，但那个半胱氨酸得先在 DNA 上装进去。<b>Sortase A（认 LPXTG）、SpyTag</b> 更专一，可每一个都要一段<b>基因编码的识别标签</b>。<b>绕一圈还是回 DNA。</b>（这一整段在 beyondPoints。）'},
 {n:'02', t:'这是一件什么工作',
  big:'把<b>一段基因</b>和<b>一个载体</b>接成一个能在细胞里复制的环。之后的一切只服务三件事：<b>末端接得上 · 对的菌落找得出 · 接口上阅读框不乱</b>',
  en:'“Cloning here means joining a gene to a vector so that the joined circle replicates inside a cell. A vector is a DNA molecule that carries a passenger and replicates on its own. The minimal plasmid is an origin of replication plus an antibiotic resistance gene, and nothing else is strictly required. Everything else on it serves one of three jobs. The ends have to join, the right colony has to be findable, and the reading frame across the junction has to survive.”',
  note:'<b>两个承重词在第一句就交代掉</b>：<b>vector</b>（带客人、自己能复制的那个 DNA 分子）和 <b>origin of replication</b>（复制从哪里开始的那个位置）。不交代它们，「克隆」这个词就是空的。<br><b>三件事就是这张卡的三个大段</b>：末端怎么配上（点 07–11）· 磷酸账（点 12–13）· 选还是筛（点 14–16）。'},
 {n:'03', t:'整张卡的脊梁',
  big:'每一种方法都在回答<b>同一个问题</b>：怎么让两段 DNA 的末端<b>互相找得到</b>。它们的区别<b>只在于什么让末端配得上</b>',
  en:'“Every cloning method is answering the same question. How do I make two pieces of DNA carry ends that will find each other? The methods differ only in what makes those ends compatible. Once I can say what makes the ends match, a method I have never used still has a place to sit.”',
  note:'⚠ <b>这句话幻灯片上没有。</b>笔记每一节各自讲了自己的末端化学，<b>把它们排成一条轴是我自己的整理</b>。说的时候说「这是我把它们串起来的方式」，别说「老师讲过」。<br><b>但它不是我硬加的</b>：笔记最后一节（1-19）自己说这道题的答案是一个<b>选择</b>，而不是一份清单——<b>一条轴正是那一节要的东西</b>。<span class="pg">L2 s.33</span>',
  good:'好处是<b>一个没见过的方法也放得进去</b>。问它两句就够：<b>末端是谁做出来的？做出来之后是谁把它封上的？</b>这两句跟纯化那张卡上的两句（抓什么 / 放什么）是同一种用法。'},
 {n:'04', t:'四个答案',
  big:'末端的来处只有<b>四种</b>：<b>位点里面切 · 位点外面切 · 外切酶啃出单链 · 根本不切</b>。课上每一种方法都落在其中一格',
  en:'“There are four answers. A cut inside the recognition site, so the overhang is the one the enzyme dictates. A cut outside the recognition site, so the overhang is whatever I designed. A chewed back single strand, long enough to anneal without help. Or a recombinase, which needs no cut at all. Classical restriction cloning is the first. Golden Gate is the second. Gibson and ligation independent cloning are the third. Gateway is the fourth.”',
  note:'<b>TA 和 TOPO 是第五格，而且它最能说明这条轴管用</b>：那两个末端不是被切出来的，是<b>聚合酶多加的一个碱基</b>。放不进前四格，恰恰说明这条轴问的是对的问题——<b>末端从哪儿来</b>。',
  tbl:{head:['末端怎么来的','方法','末端长什么样','谁把它封上'], rows:[['位点<b>里面</b>切开','经典酶切克隆（Type IIP）','酶自己定的黏末端','T4 连接酶'],['位点<b>外面</b>切开','Golden Gate（Type IIS）','4 个碱基，序列你定','T4 连接酶，同一管'],['外切酶啃出单链','LIC · Gibson','约 15 nt · 20–40 bp','LIC 不封，细胞修 / Gibson 用 Taq 连接酶'],['聚合酶多加一个碱基','TA · TOPO TA','单个 3′-A 配单个 3′-T','T4 连接酶 / 拓扑异构酶自己'],['<b>根本不切</b>','Gateway','att 重组位点','重组酶自己做这个化学']]}},

 {g:'基因从哪来', gn:'动手之前先问一句：<b>这一步能不能不做。</b>四条路按从便宜到贵排，而其中一条藏着这一章最经典的考题。'},
 {n:'05', t:'四条路，按便宜到贵',
  big:'<b>查文献问作者 → Addgene → RT-PCR → 全基因合成。</b>前两条能省掉几个月已经有人做过的活',
  en:'“Four routes, and it is worth taking them cheapest first. Somebody may already have cloned the protein, and in principle the authors are obliged to send the clone, because material sharing is a condition of publishing in most journals. That saves cloning, sequencing, host optimisation and purification development. Next is a repository. Addgene holds about a hundred thousand reagents and you mostly pay shipping, roughly eighty dollars a clone. Third is RT-PCR, which you need when the exact sequence is unknown. Fourth is gene synthesis, which costs the most and gives complete control over the sequence.”',
  note:'欧洲的对应物是 <b>plasmids.eu</b>。合成的细节：<b>序列完全由你定</b>（要哪个限制位点、要什么末端都可以指定，到货就能直接进你选的那套克隆）、<b>100% 测序验证</b>、<b>可以按宿主先做密码子优化</b>、原则上大小不限但实践中<b>一般在 8 kbp 以下</b>。<b>唯一写出来的缺点是价格。</b>两档：克隆好并验证过的贵、<b>DNA strings</b> 便宜但不保证正确要自己测。供应商 GenScript、ThermoFisher、IDT。毒素和生物战剂会被筛掉，不给做。<span class="pg">L1 s.22–26</span>',
  good:'<b>密码子优化之所以做得成，唯一的理由是遗传密码简并</b>——换同义密码子，蛋白序列一个字母不变。没优化会怎样：人源基因里有些密码子在大肠杆菌里很稀有，<b>核糖体等稀缺的 tRNA 而停顿</b>，结果是低产量、截短和移码。⚠ 但有一条反直觉的要备着：<b>全部换成最常用的密码子不一定最好</b>，有些稀有密码子造成的停顿是<b>共翻译折叠</b>需要的；优化还得避开意外造出的限制位点和核糖体结合位点附近的强二级结构。（这一整段在 beyondPoints。）<b>稀有密码子的对策 Rosetta 菌株在卡 pe-expr。</b>'},
 {n:'06', t:'⚠ 内含子 · 这一章最经典的一道题',
  big:'<b>真核基因组 DNA 里有内含子，原核没有剪接体。</b>直接从基因组扩出来放进大肠杆菌，表达出来是废的',
  en:'“A classic question is why a eukaryotic gene cannot simply be amplified from genomic DNA and expressed in E. coli. The answer is introns. Prokaryotes have no spliceosome, so the introns are transcribed and translated along with the exons and the product is nonsense. RT-PCR solves it by starting from mature spliced messenger RNA and reverse transcribing that into cDNA. The cDNA is intron free by construction rather than by luck, because the cell did the splicing before I touched it.”',
  note:'<b>“intron free by construction rather than by luck” 这个说法值得原样说出口。</b><br>笔记说 RT-PCR「old-fashioned 但仍然广泛使用」，而它<b>不可替代的场合只有一个</b>：<b>不知道确切序列</b>的时候——合成需要一个能填进订单的序列，RT-PCR 只需要那块组织。<span class="pg">L1 s.24</span><br><b>逆转录酶属于哪一族聚合酶，接卡 taq。</b>'},

 {g:'四族方法 · 一族一格', gn:'<b>每一格只答两句</b>：末端是怎么来的，谁把它封上。名字、年份、酶名都挂在这两句下面，不要反过来。'},
 {n:'07', t:'第一族 · 切在位点里面（经典酶切克隆）',
  big:'七步。位点写在<b>引物尾巴</b>上，酶切在<b>识别位点里面</b>，所以<b>黏末端的序列是酶定的，不是你定的</b>',
  en:'“Classical restriction cloning is seven steps. Amplify the gene by PCR with restriction sites added in the primer tails. Cut the insert. Cut the plasmid with complementary enzymes. Dephosphorylate the plasmid if needed. Ligate. Transform. Select the positive colonies. The enzymes are type two P enzymes such as EcoRI, BamHI, HindIII and NotI. They recognise a palindrome and cut inside it, so the overhang sequence is dictated entirely by the enzyme.”',
  note:'Type IIP 占实际使用的约 <b>90%</b>。<b>限制酶 1971–1973 年被描述</b>，重组 DNA 作为一个领域就是从这里开始的。已知 <b>3000 多种</b>酶，识别约 <b>350 种</b>基序。它们原本是细菌防御噬菌体的武器，细菌靠<b>甲基化</b>保护自己的 DNA。连接条件：<b>16 °C 过夜，或室温 10 分钟</b>。<span class="pg">L2 s.9–10 · L2 s.15</span>',
  warn:'⚠ <b>两个设计要点全在引物尾巴上。</b>① <b>填充碱基</b>：限制酶在线性片段的<b>最末端</b>切得很差，所以位点外面还要加几个碱基，每家供应商都印了一张「靠近末端的切割」表。② <b>阅读框</b>：只要做融合（标签、信号肽），接口的框就必须对上。<br>⚠ 第三个是<b>看不见</b>的失败：<b>甲基化</b>。质粒图上位点在、NEBcutter 也说在，酶就是不切——因为 DH5α、TOP10 都是 <b>Dam⁺ Dcm⁺</b>，而 XbaI、ClaI、MboI 的位点压在 GATC 上时会被 Dam 甲基化挡住。<b>办法是先在 dam⁻ dcm⁻ 菌株里扩一遍再切。</b>酶切失败的排查顺序是<b>甲基化 → 切得离末端太近 → 缓冲液和星号活性</b>，<b>甲基化排第一正因为图看上去完全正常</b>。（这一条在 beyondPoints。）'},
 {n:'08', t:'第二族 · 切在位点外面（Golden Gate）',
  big:'<b>Type IIS 酶切在识别位点外面。</b>两件事同时成立：<b>位点不进产物（所以无疤痕）</b>，<b>4 碱基末端的序列由你定（所以能一次定向拼多段）</b>',
  en:'“Golden Gate uses type two S enzymes, BsaI, BbsI and BsmBI. The defining property is that they cut outside their own recognition sequence. Two things follow from that one fact. The four base overhang has a sequence I choose rather than one the enzyme dictates, and four bases give two hundred and fifty six possibilities. And the recognition site itself sits on the small piece that is thrown away, so it never appears in the product. Plasmid, up to ten inserts and T4 ligase all go into a single tube.”',
  note:'<b>一锅切、一锅连能成立，靠的是一个棘轮。</b>切和连同时进行，在约 <b>37 °C</b> 切和 <b>16 °C</b> 连之间循环。<b>接对了的接口把识别位点毁掉了</b>（位点在被丢掉的那一小段上），所以再也切不开，产物被<b>困住</b>；接错的、或者自己连回去的载体<b>把位点重新造了出来</b>，被再切一次，回到池子里。<b>20–40 个循环下来，反应被不可逆地推向全对的那个产物</b>，5–10 个片段也常在 <b>90% 以上</b>。<b>它成立不是因为化学有选择性，是因为错的可逆、对的不可逆。</b>（这段在 beyondPoints。）<span class="pg">L2 s.20–21</span>',
  warn:'⚠ <b>入场费叫 domestication。</b>用之前必须把每个部件内部的 BsaI / BbsI / BsmBI 位点全部去掉，否则反应里它们会被切碎、拼出截短的东西。去掉的办法是<b>沉默突变</b>——换密码子不换氨基酸，<b>这一招之所以可行，又是因为遗传密码简并</b>。这是<b>一次性成本</b>，付过之后部件永远可重用，这正是 <b>MoClo、GoldenBraid 2.0、Mobius Assembly、EMMA</b> 这些标准件库存在的理由，笔记管它们叫 plasmid LEGOs。<br>⚠ <b>256 是理论上限，不是能同时用的数。</b>回文末端会自连，差一个碱基的末端会错连。NEB 的 Potapov 等人 2018 年（ACS Synth. Biol. 7:2665）测了全部四碱基末端的连接保真度矩阵，现在用设计工具挑高保真组合，<b>挑得好一次能拼二十个以上</b>。（这两条都在 beyondPoints。）'},
 {n:'09', t:'第三族 · 啃出来的单链（LIC 与 Gibson）',
  big:'两个都是<b>把一条链啃掉，露出很长的单链</b>。<b>末端长到退火本身就够稳</b>，所以 LIC <b>连连接酶都不需要</b>',
  en:'“Ligation independent cloning and Gibson assembly both work by chewing one strand back to expose a long single strand. In LIC the enzyme is T4 DNA polymerase running as an exonuclease, and it is stopped at a designed position by supplying only one of the four nucleotides. The overhang is about fifteen bases. Two overhangs that long anneal stably enough that no ligase is needed, so the annealed product is transformed directly and the cell repairs the two nicks. Gibson uses T5 exonuclease instead, with overlaps of twenty to forty base pairs, and it runs at fifty degrees in one tube.”',
  note:'<b>LIC 的单 dNTP 花招</b>：T4 DNA 聚合酶有两个活性——需要模板引物和 dNTP 的 <b>5′→3′ 聚合</b>，和很强的、不依赖模板的 <b>3′→5′ 外切</b>。<b>管子里放什么核苷酸，决定哪一个活性占上风。</b>把 LIC 尾巴（约 <b>12–18 碱基</b>）设计成整段缺一种碱基，比如上链尾巴里没有 G，然后<b>只加 dGTP</b>：外切一路啃，啃到<b>第一个该切掉 G 的位置</b>就停住，因为聚合酶立刻用管里的 dGTP 把它补回去，酶卡在那一个碱基上空转。<b>末端的位置因此是被设计出来的，不是被切出来的。</b>跟限制酶留下的 4 个碱基比，<b>15 个碱基的退火稳定性高好几个数量级</b>。（这段在 beyondPoints。）<span class="pg">L2 s.29–30</span>',
  good:'<b>Gibson 三个酶同管、同一个 50 °C，先后顺序靠的是热稳定性的差异，不是分步加料。</b><b>T5 外切酶不耐热</b>，啃出单链之后自己失活退场，来不及破坏已经退火好的产物；<b>Phusion</b> 补缺口；<b>Taq 连接酶</b>封 nick——<b>是 Taq 不是 T4，因为 T4 在 50 °C 会变性</b>。2009 年 Gibson 等人发在 Nature Methods 上。效率对 <b>15 kb 以下</b>的质粒约 <b>90%</b>，NEBuilder HiFi 能容忍 <b>16–20 bp</b> 的短重叠和高 GC 接口。（三个酶为什么不打架在 beyondPoints；<b>幻灯片自己只给了一条注意：拼缝要测序</b>。）',
  warn:'⚠ <b>LIC 的代价是接头序列不自由</b>：停住的位置是靠「整段缺一种碱基」造出来的，所以尾巴的序列你不能随便写。<b>Gibson 完全没有这个限制</b>——<b>这就是 Gibson 基本取代 LIC 的原因</b>，也是它能用来拼合成基因组的原因（Venter 研究所用的就是它）。<b>In-Fusion</b> 是 LIC 的商业版，用<b>牛痘 3′→5′ 外切酶</b>代替 T4 DNA 聚合酶，配 Stellar 感受态细胞（大肠杆菌 BW23474）。'},
 {n:'10', t:'第四族 · 根本不切（Gateway）',
  big:'<b>不用限制酶，也不用连接酶。</b>借的是 λ 噬菌体的<b>位点特异性重组</b>。>95% 的阳性率来自<b>双重选择</b>，代价是<b>八个残基的疤</b>',
  en:'“Gateway uses no restriction enzyme and no ligase at all. It borrows the site specific recombination that phage lambda uses to integrate into the E. coli chromosome. BP clonase is integrase plus integration host factor, and it turns attB and attP into attL and attR. LR clonase adds excisionase and runs the reaction back the other way. The efficiency is above ninety five per cent, and that comes from two independent filters. The destination vector carries a different antibiotic resistance, and it also carries the ccdB toxin gene in the slot my gene will occupy.”',
  note:'att 位点的长度：<b>attB 25 nt · attP 243 nt · attL 100 nt · attR 168 nt</b>。供体载体是 <b>pDONR221</b>，BP 反应把基因放进去做成 entry clone，LR 反应把它转进目的表达载体。<b>λ 整合酶和切除酶就是核酸酶那一节里的「特异内切酶」</b>——<b>Gateway 卖的就是那两个酶装在管子里</b>。<span class="pg">L2 s.22–25 · L1 s.28</span><br><b>正选择和负选择的定义要背准</b>：<b>正选择 ＝ 想要的活下来</b>（没质粒就没抗性，死在抗生素上）；<b>负选择 ＝ 不想要的死掉</b>（没重组的载体还在表达 ccdB，自己毒死自己）。<b>Gateway 两层一起用，这就是 >95% 的来源。</b>ccdB 抑制的是 <b>DNA 旋转酶</b>，也就是细菌的 II 型拓扑异构酶，它切开双链来解超螺旋，是活不下去就不行的那种酶——同一个道理让它在人身上成为化疗靶点。<span class="pg">L2 s.8</span>',
  warn:'⚠ <b>八个残基的疤不是脚注，是死穴。</b>attB 位点留在最终构建体里，<b>而且会被翻译</b>，在融合接口上多出约 <b>8 个氨基酸</b>。常规表达纯化无所谓；<b>要真实 N 端、要解晶体结构、要研究信号肽或蛋白酶切位点时，它改掉的正是你要研究的那段序列</b>。<b>题面里一出现 authentic N-terminus 或 scarless，Gateway 就是要被明确排除的那一个</b>，换 Golden Gate、Gibson、LIC 或 In-Fusion。（这条在 beyondPoints。）<br>⚠ 连带的一条：<b>带 ccdB 的目的载体自己没法在普通菌株里扩</b>，它会把宿主毒死。要用 <b>DB3.1</b> 或 <b>ccdB Survival</b>，那里的旋转酶是突变过的、CcdB 抓不住。JM109、XL1-Blue、XL10-Gold 天然带 F 质粒，所以<b>部分</b>耐受。'},
 {n:'11', t:'第五格 · 末端来自聚合酶（TA 与 TOPO TA）',
  big:'末端不是切出来的，是<b>聚合酶多加的</b>：<b>Taq 给 PCR 产物每一端加一个 3′-A</b>，配一个带 3′-T 的线性载体。<b>全程不需要酶切</b>',
  en:'“TA cloning uses a side activity of Taq polymerase. Taq has a terminal transferase activity that adds a single three prime A overhang to each end of the PCR product, without any template. That product is ligated straight into a linearised vector carrying single three prime T overhangs. No restriction digest happens at any point. TOPO TA replaces the ligase with vaccinia topoisomerase one, supplied already attached to the vector, and the reaction takes five minutes at room temperature.”',
  note:'<b>能量藏在哪里</b>：牛痘拓扑异构酶 I 认 <b>5′-(C/T)CCTT-3′</b>，切开一条链，并在自己活性位点的<b>酪氨酸</b>和 DNA 的 3′-磷酸之间形成一个<b>共价磷酸酪氨酸键</b>——<b>被切断的那个磷酸二酯键的能量存进了这个蛋白–DNA 连接里，没有丢掉</b>。插入片段的 5′-羟基一进攻，酶就把自己释放出去，键重新形成。<b>不需要 ATP，不需要连接酶</b>——这就是为什么它是室温五分钟，而不是 16 °C 过夜。（这段在 beyondPoints。）<b>磷酸二酯键本身接卡 03 和 x-bonds。</b><span class="pg">L2 s.26–28</span>',
  warn:'⚠ <b>三个代价。</b>① <b>不定向</b>：两端都是 A、载体两端都是 T，插进去正反都行，还得筛（定向版的 TOPO 存在，专门解决这一条）。② <b>连接效率低</b>于设计过的黏末端，而且线性载体得买。③ <b>被迫用 Taq</b>——Pfu、Phusion 这些带校对的酶给的是<b>平末端</b>，根本不工作。<b>所以 TA 克隆天生绑着低保真的那个酶</b>：对一段反正要测序的片段没关系，对一个要拿去表达的构建体就不好。真要两样都要，就用 Phusion 扩完再拿 <b>Taq 加 dATP</b> 短孵一下补 A，叫 <b>A-tailing</b>。（这一条在 beyondPoints。）<b>校对活性和保真度接卡 taq。</b>'},

 {g:'磷酸账 · 一条规则解释一半的步骤', gn:'这一段是整套克隆里<b>最省力的杠杆</b>：记住连接酶要什么，流程里一堆看着随意的步骤立刻变得显然。'},
 {n:'12', t:'连接酶只要一件事',
  big:'<b>5′-磷酸 ＋ 3′-羟基，两个都得在场。</b>缺哪一个，那个接口就连不上',
  en:'“T4 DNA ligase forms a phosphodiester bond between juxtaposed five prime phosphate and three prime hydroxyl termini. Both have to be present. If I track the phosphates through a protocol, several steps that look arbitrary become obvious. Restriction enzymes leave a five prime phosphate, so a freshly cut vector and insert ligate directly with no extra treatment. Synthetic oligonucleotides are made with a five prime hydroxyl instead, so a PCR product made with ordinary primers cannot be ligated at that end.”',
  note:'补救办法两个：<b>订 5′ 磷酸化的引物</b>，或者用 <b>T4 多核苷酸激酶（PNK）</b>把 ATP 上的磷酸转到 5′-羟基上。磷酸酶是 <b>SAP（虾碱性磷酸酶）、CIP（小牛肠磷酸酶）、南极磷酸酶</b>，非特异地去掉 DNA 和 RNA 两端的磷酸单酯，顺带也水解 NTP 和 dNTP。<span class="pg">L1 s.28</span><br><b>连接酶和核酸酶各属于哪一类反应，接卡 x-rxn；它做的那个磷酸二酯键接卡 03 和 x-bonds。</b>',
  good:'<b>核酸酶分三族，一句话记法：内切从中间切，外切从末端啃。</b>① <b>特异内切酶</b>＝限制酶，外加 <b>λ 整合酶和切除酶</b>（Gateway 卖的就是这两个）。② <b>非特异内切酶</b>：<b>RNase H</b> 只水解<b>杂合在 DNA 上的</b> RNA，所以逆转录之后拿它去掉 RNA 链；<b>DNase I</b> 双链单链 DNA 都降；<b>微球菌核酸酶</b>连 RNA 一起降，留下 3′-磷酸的寡核苷酸。③ <b>外切酶</b>：<b>T5 外切酶</b>就是 Gibson 的引擎，<b>外切酶 I</b> 只啃单链，<b>聚合酶的校对活性也归这一族</b>。<b>这一节看着像目录，其实是在给后面每一种方法发零件。</b>'},
 {n:'13', t:'⚠ 磷酸酶是记账，不是化学',
  big:'给载体去磷酸，<b>是为了让它自己合不上</b>。空载体自连的转化效率极高，是<b>背景菌落最大的来源</b>',
  en:'“A vector cut with a single enzyme has two complementary ends, so it can simply religate to itself. Empty self ligated vector transforms extremely efficiently, and it is the single biggest source of background colonies. Removing the vector five prime phosphates makes that impossible, because ligase needs a five prime phosphate on at least one side of each nick. The insert still carries its own phosphates, so the real vector and insert junctions still form, leaving two nicks that the cell repairs after transformation.”',
  note:'⚠ <b>「记账不是化学」这个说法是我自己的</b>，但它说的正是笔记的意思：磷酸酶<b>没有改变连接反应的化学</b>，它只是把一边的<b>记账项抹掉</b>，让那一边永远凑不齐「5′-磷酸 ＋ 3′-羟基」。<b>所以它是点 12 那条规则的一次故意使用，而不是一个新机制。</b><span class="pg">L2 s.15</span>',
  warn:'⚠ <b>有一种情况不该做。</b>如果你用的是<b>两个末端互不相容的酶做的定向双酶切</b>，载体本来就自连不了，去磷酸化只会白白损失效率。<b>定向克隆是同一个问题的更好解法</b>，而且它多给你一样东西：<b>插入片段的方向被固定死了</b>。（这条在 beyondPoints。）<br><b>所以完整的答法是两句</b>：先说它解决什么问题，再说什么时候这个问题已经不存在了。'},

 {g:'哪个菌落是对的 · 选 vs 筛', gn:'<b>选（selection）是让错的活不成，筛（screening）是让错的看得出来。</b>这一组的三个陷阱全部踩在「把筛当成选」上。'},
 {n:'14', t:'载体本身 · ORI 决定拷贝数',
  big:'最小的质粒只要<b>一个复制起点 ＋ 一个抗性基因</b>。<b>ORI 决定拷贝数</b>，而且<b>相同 ORI 的两个质粒不能共存于一个细胞</b>',
  en:'“A plasmid is a small circular DNA molecule replicating independently of the chromosome, typically fifteen hundred to twenty thousand base pairs. The minimal plasmid is an origin of replication plus an antibiotic resistance gene. The origin is where replication starts. It is rich in A and T so the strands separate more easily, and the replication itself is done by host proteins rather than by anything the plasmid encodes. The origin also sets the copy number.”',
  note:'⚠ <b>反直觉的那条要记牢</b>：<b>克隆质粒是高拷贝的</b>（pUC 用突变的 pMB1，<b>500–700</b> 份；pBluescript 用突变的 ColE1 和 F1，300–500 份），<b>表达质粒反而是低拷贝的</b>（pET 和 pGEX 都用 pBR322，只有 <b>15–20</b> 份）。理由是<b>代谢负担</b>：拷贝数太高，细胞的资源全花在复制质粒和转录外源基因上，长得差、表达反而更少、甚至把质粒整个丢掉。<b>克隆质粒唯一的任务是产量，所以越高越好；表达质粒不是。</b>（这条解释在 beyondPoints。）<span class="pg">L2 s.4–6</span><br><b>相同 ORI 不相容这条，以及 pDUET 为什么存在，在卡 pe-expr。</b>',
  good:'<b>克隆菌株为什么写成 recA⁻ endA⁻</b>：<b>RecA</b> 驱动同源重组，在 recA⁺ 里，带重复序列的质粒会跟自己重组、把两段重复之间的东西<b>悄悄删掉</b>，构建体变了你还不知道；<b>EndA</b> 是周质核酸酶，做 miniprep 时把 DNA 降解掉，产量低、拖尾、测序难看。DH5α、TOP10、DH10b、XL1-Blue 都是这两样都缺的。（这两条在 beyondPoints。）'},
 {n:'15', t:'⚠ 卫星菌落不是转化子',
  big:'β-内酰胺酶是<b>分泌出去</b>的。它把菌落周围琼脂里的氨苄破坏掉，<b>不带质粒的细胞就在那一圈里长出来了</b>',
  en:'“Ampicillin resistance works through beta lactamase, which degrades the beta lactam ring. The enzyme is secreted into the periplasm and leaks into the medium, so it destroys ampicillin in a halo around each resistant colony. Cells with no plasmid can then grow as tiny satellite colonies inside that cleared zone. If I pick one, I get no plasmid at all. The fixes are to use carbenicillin, which resists the enzyme better, or simply not to over incubate the plate and to pick only well isolated colonies.”',
  note:'<b>卡那霉素没有这个问题</b>，因为它的抗性酶（氨基糖苷-3′-磷酸转移酶）<b>在细胞里工作</b>，它<b>修饰药物</b>，而不是把培养基里的药整批清掉。<b>这是大多数 pET 质粒用卡那做标记的一个很实在的理由。</b>（这一条在 beyondPoints。）<span class="pg">L2 s.7–8</span>',
  good:'那张抗生素表只有一条线索要记：<b>靶点决定适用范围。</b>打细菌<b>核糖体</b>的（30S：卡那、四环素、大观霉素、庆大；50S：氯霉素）或打<b>细胞壁</b>的（氨苄）<b>只对原核有效</b>；<b>潮霉素 B、杀稻瘟菌素、Zeocin 不依赖细菌特有的结构，所以原核真核通杀</b>——<b>这正是做哺乳动物稳定株只能用这三个的原因</b>。（Zeocin 还有个漂亮的机制：铜络合态是失活的，进细胞后铜被还原，药才活过来，而抗性蛋白 Sh ble 以 1:1 把它扣住。）'},
 {n:'16', t:'⚠ 蓝白斑报告的是「插进去了」，不是「插对了」',
  big:'<b>蓝 ＝ 空载体，白 ＝ 有插入。</b>但白色<b>只证明 lacZ-α 被打断了</b>——方向对不对、序列对不对，它一个字都没说',
  en:'“Blue white screening works by alpha complementation of beta galactosidase. The large omega fragment is on the chromosome, and the small alpha fragment of fifty nine residues is on the plasmid with the cloning site sitting inside it. Cells are plated on agar containing X gal and IPTG. An empty vector gives an intact alpha fragment, the two fragments complement, active beta galactosidase cleaves X gal into a blue insoluble product, and the colony is blue. An insert disrupts the alpha fragment, so there is no complementation and the colony stays white.”',
  note:'<b>IPTG 在这里干什么</b>：lacZ-α 是由 <b>lac 启动子</b>驱动的，不诱导就什么都不表达，<b>所有菌落都会是白的</b>，蓝白斑就废了。<b>这就是为什么平板上必须同时有 X-gal 和 IPTG。</b><b>lac 操纵子、LacI、别乳糖那一整套在卡 12——蓝白斑读的就是那套开关。</b><br>还有一个前提：<b>质粒和菌株要配对</b>，比如 pUC19 配 lacZ 突变的 DH5α 或 XL1-Blue。<span class="pg">L2 s.16–17</span>',
  warn:'⚠ <b>白色之后仍然要菌落 PCR 或测序。</b>笔记的前提句是「<b>克隆不是 100% 有效率的</b>」，所以确认这一步从来不能省。两条路：<b>直接做菌落 PCR</b>，或者<b>提 DNA 再酶切或测序</b>。<b>把「蓝白斑只报告插入，不报告正确」这句主动说出来，比等他来挑值钱得多。</b>（这半条在 beyondPoints。）',
  good:'顺手能给一句<b>为什么 β-半乳糖苷酶劈成两半还能工作</b>：它要<b>四聚</b>才有活性，而介导四聚的正是<b>蛋白 N 端那一段</b>——α 片段就是那一段。<b>所以 α-互补不是巧合，是这个酶的装配方式允许的。</b>'},

 {g:'怎么选 · 这张卡的落点', gn:'笔记最后一节问的就是这句话。<b>只背决策表反而答不完整</b>，因为幻灯片自己给的是另一个答案。'},
 {n:'17', t:'三个问题，再加一句幻灯片自己的答案',
  big:'<b>接口要不要干净？ · 要拼几段？ · 有没有硬约束？</b>答完三句，再加一句<b>「实际上你用的是实验室已经在跑的那一套」</b>',
  en:'“I would work through three questions. First, does the junction have to be clean? If I need an authentic N terminus, or a crystal structure, or I am studying a signal peptide, then Gateway is out and I use a scarless method. Second, what shape is the assembly? One insert with usable sites is plain restriction cloning, standardised parts are Golden Gate, one gene into many vectors is Gateway, and several large fragments are Gibson. Third, is there a hard constraint? If every enzyme in the cloning site also cuts inside my gene, I go to Gibson or LIC, because neither depends on restriction enzymes.”',
  note:'⚠ <b>只背这张决策表，答得反而不完整。</b>幻灯片自己给的答案是另一句：<b>实际上你用的是实验室已经在跑的那一套</b>——因为优化好的流程、积累下来的经验、货架上现成的那批限制酶、以及标准化的表达质粒集都在那里。大研究中心还有<b>专门做克隆和表达的 core facility</b>：高通量、省钱，而且把你解放出来做真正不平凡的那部分。<b>考官问这道题，一半是在看你知不知道约束既是技术上的也是现实上的。</b><span class="pg">L2 s.33</span><br>查位点的工具：<b>NEBcutter</b> 免费就够（Webcutter、Expasy 也行），商业套件是 SnapGene、DNAStar Lasergene、Vector NTI，<b>Benchling 现在是学术界事实上的免费标准</b>（Benchling 和 SnapGene Viewer 这两句在 beyondPoints）。<span class="pg">L2 s.3</span>',
  good:'<b>题面里的关键词直接映射到方法</b>：<b>synthetic biology / multi-fragment / standardised parts → Golden Gate</b>；<b>one gene into several expression vectors → Gateway</b>（并且主动说你接受那八个残基）；<b>authentic N-terminus / scarless → Gibson、LIC、In-Fusion</b>，并且<b>明确把 Gateway 排除掉</b>；<b>没有任何可用的限制位点 → Gibson 或 LIC</b>；<b>先随便存一下回头再亚克隆 → TOPO TA</b>；<b>拼很长的片段或整个基因组 → Gibson</b>。（这张映射表在 beyondPoints。）'},
 {n:'18', t:'⚠ 设计题丢分最集中的两处',
  big:'<b>位点没在插入片段里查过</b>，和<b>接口处凭空冒出一个终止密码子</b>。两处都是「纸上看着对、台面上一定失败」',
  en:'“Two mistakes lose most of the marks on a design question. The first is picking sites from the cloning site of the vector without checking the insert. An enzyme that also cuts inside my gene would fragment my own insert during the digest, so I run the gene through NEBcutter first and intersect the two lists. The second is the reading frame across the junction. A spacer has to put the downstream tag in frame, and it must not create a stop codon together with the sequence on either side of it.”',
  note:'那道 <b>pSecTag2</b> 的练习就是照这两条设计的。载体 MCS 上有十一个酶，把插入片段过一遍 NEBcutter 之后<b>只剩三个</b>（SfiI、AscI、EcoRV），选 <b>AscI ＋ EcoRV</b> 两个不同的酶，于是克隆是<b>定向</b>的。基因被夹在 <b>Igκ leader → 你的基因 → myc → 六聚组氨酸 → 终止</b>之间，<b>两端都必须同框</b>：跟 leader 不同框，信号肽后面接的是乱码，什么都分泌不出去；跟标签不同框，就没有 His 标签，纯化不了。<b>而且插入片段自己的终止密码子必须去掉</b>，否则翻译在够到标签之前就停了。载体分 A/B/C 三个版本，差的就是 MCS 里一两个碱基，<b>差别的全部作用就是移动阅读框</b>——这道题的答案是 <b>A</b>。<span class="pg">L2 s.35–43</span>',
  warn:'⚠ <b>幻灯片第 42 张那个陷阱单独记。</b>间隔碱基如果取 <b>TA</b>，跨接口读过去是 …aag gca ＋ <b>TA</b> ＋ <b>GAT</b>ATC，在框里正好拼出 <b>TAG</b>，一个<b>琥珀终止密码子</b>，就坐在标签前面。<b>蛋白照样造出来、照样分泌出去，但完全纯化不了</b>，而你要好几周才发现。<b>所以间隔碱基必须连着两侧的序列一起查，不能单看它自己</b>，TAA 和 TGA 也一样。<br>⚠ 还有最便宜的一分：<b>反向引物写出来是正义链方向的，订之前必须反向互补</b>。照着抄上订单，你拿到的寡核苷酸什么都不结合。（这两条都在 beyondPoints。）',
  good:'<b>一句能显出你把整门课当一件事读的话</b>：<b>TAG 这个琥珀密码子，正是第 7、8 讲里被重新指派去掺入非天然氨基酸的那一个。</b>在这道题里它是毁掉构建体的 bug，在那里它是整个功能本身。'}
],

end:'<b>这张卡的用法：</b>无论他问哪一种方法，先报那条脊梁——<b>所有方法都在回答同一个问题，怎么让两段 DNA 的末端互相找得到，区别只在什么让末端配得上</b>。然后只讲他问的那一族，<b>不要五种一起倒</b>。四个陷阱随时准备好：<b>卫星菌落不是转化子 · 白斑只报告插入不报告正确 · Type IIS 切在位点外面所以 Golden Gate 无疤痕 · 磷酸酶是记账不是化学</b>。',

sib:[
['<b>脊梁</b>：每种方法都在回答「怎么让两段 DNA 的末端互相找得到」，区别只在<b>什么让末端配得上</b>',
 '“Every cloning method answers the same question. How do I make two pieces of DNA carry ends that will find each other? They differ only in what makes those ends compatible.”',
 '<b>整张卡的骨架。</b>先给这一句，他后面无论问哪个方法，你都已经有位置放它了。⚠ 这是我自己的整理，不是幻灯片的话。'],
['<b>四个答案</b>：位点<b>里面</b>切 · 位点<b>外面</b>切 · 外切酶<b>啃</b>出单链 · <b>根本不切</b>（重组酶）',
 '“A cut inside the recognition site, a cut outside it, a chewed back single strand, or a recombinase that needs no cut at all.”',
 '分别是<b>经典酶切 · Golden Gate · Gibson 和 LIC · Gateway</b>。第五格是 TA/TOPO：末端来自<b>聚合酶</b>，不是来自切。'],
['<b>Type IIS 切在识别位点外面</b> → 位点不进产物（无疤痕）＋ 4 碱基末端序列由你定（可定向拼多段）',
 '“Type two S enzymes cut outside their own recognition sequence. So the site ends up on the discarded piece and never appears in the product, and the four base overhang has a sequence I choose.”',
 '<b>Golden Gate 的一切都来自这一条。</b>256 个可能的末端是理论上限，实际要用工具挑高保真组合。'],
['<b>Gibson 三个酶同管 50 °C</b>：T5 外切酶啃 → Phusion 补 → <b>Taq</b> 连接酶封。顺序靠<b>热稳定性差异</b>',
 '“T5 exonuclease is heat labile, so it makes the overhangs and then inactivates itself before it can destroy the annealed product. Phusion fills the gaps and the thermostable Taq ligase seals the nicks.”',
 '⚠ <b>是 Taq 连接酶不是 T4</b>，因为 T4 在 50 °C 会变性。「为什么三个酶不打架」是这一节最可能被追的地方。'],
['<b>LIC</b>：T4 DNA 聚合酶跑外切，<b>只给一种 dNTP</b> 把它停在设计好的位置，末端约 15 nt，<b>不要连接酶</b>',
 '“Two fifteen base overhangs anneal stably enough that no ligase is needed. You transform the annealed product directly and the cell repairs the two nicks.”',
 '代价是<b>尾巴序列不自由</b>（必须整段缺一种碱基）。<b>Gibson 没有这个限制，所以取代了它。</b>'],
['<b>Gateway</b>：λ 的位点特异性重组，<b>不用限制酶也不用连接酶</b>。>95% 来自<b>双重选择</b>，代价是 <b>8 个残基的疤</b>',
 '“BP clonase turns attB and attP into attL and attR, and LR clonase runs it back. The destination vector carries a different antibiotic and the ccdB toxin, so two filters act at once.”',
 '⚠ <b>题面一出现 authentic N-terminus 或 scarless，Gateway 就是要被排除的那一个。</b>'],
['<b>正选择 ＝ 想要的活下来</b>（抗生素）；<b>负选择 ＝ 不想要的死掉</b>（空载体还在表达 ccdB，自己毒死自己）',
 '“Positive selection means only the cells I want survive. Negative selection means the cells I do not want are actively killed.”',
 '<b>Gateway 把两层叠在一起用，这就是 95% 的来源。</b>带 ccdB 的载体自己要在 DB3.1 里扩。'],
['<b>连接酶只要一件事</b>：<b>5′-磷酸 ＋ 3′-羟基，两个都在场</b>。克隆里一半莫名其妙的步骤都从这条推出来',
 '“T4 ligase forms a phosphodiester bond between juxtaposed five prime phosphate and three prime hydroxyl termini. Both have to be present.”',
 '酶切末端<b>自带</b>5′-磷酸；合成寡核苷酸是 5′-<b>羟基</b>，所以普通引物扩的 PCR 产物那一端连不上。'],
['⚠ <b>磷酸酶是记账不是化学</b>：抹掉载体的 5′-磷酸，它就自己合不上了。<b>定向双酶切时不该做</b>',
 '“Removing the vector five prime phosphates makes self ligation impossible, because ligase needs a five prime phosphate on at least one side of each nick.”',
 '空载体自连转化效率极高，是<b>背景菌落最大的来源</b>。但双酶切已经堵死了自连，再去磷酸只是白丢效率。'],
['⚠ <b>卫星菌落不是转化子</b>：β-内酰胺酶<b>分泌出去</b>，把菌落周围的氨苄清掉，没质粒的细胞在那圈里长出来',
 '“Beta lactamase leaks into the medium and destroys ampicillin in a halo around each colony, so cells with no plasmid grow there as satellites. If I pick one I get no plasmid.”',
 '卡那没有这个问题，它的抗性酶<b>在细胞里修饰药物</b>。这是 pET 多用卡那的实在理由。'],
['⚠ <b>白色只证明 lacZ-α 被打断了</b>：方向对不对、序列对不对，蓝白斑一个字都没说',
 '“A white colony only tells me the alpha fragment was disrupted. The orientation and the sequence still have to be confirmed by colony PCR or sequencing.”',
 '平板上 <b>X-gal ＋ IPTG</b> 缺一不可——不诱导就全白。<b>lac 那一套在卡 12。</b>'],
['⚠ <b>内含子</b>：真核基因组 DNA 直接扩来放进大肠杆菌是废的，因为<b>原核没有剪接体</b>',
 '“Prokaryotes have no spliceosome, so introns are transcribed and translated along with the exons. Starting from mature messenger RNA gives cDNA that is intron free by construction.”',
 '<b>这是这一章最经典的一道题</b>，一句话答案就是 introns。'],
['<b>怎么选</b>：接口要不要干净 → 拼几段 → 有没有硬约束。<b>再加一句：实际上用实验室已经在跑的那套</b>',
 '“The technical rule gives me a shortlist, but in practice you use the system already implemented in your lab, because that is where the protocols and the reagents and the standard vectors are.”',
 '<b>最后那句是幻灯片自己的答案。</b>只背决策表反而答得不完整。']
],

/* ---------------- 演练四段 ---------------- */
segs:[
 {tag:'段 1 · 定义', h:'先说为什么非在 DNA 上做，再说这是一件什么工作，最后给整个答案的形状',
  p:['“The product of protein engineering is a protein, so the first thing worth saying is why we go through DNA at all. The central dogma says information never passes from protein to protein or from protein to nucleic acid, so a protein cannot be templated and cannot be amplified. And there is a marked absence of tools for targeted manipulation at the protein level. So the only way to make a specific change reproducibly is to make it in the DNA.”',
     '“Cloning then means joining a gene to a vector so that the joined circle replicates inside a cell. A vector is a DNA molecule that carries a passenger and replicates on its own. The minimal plasmid is an origin of replication plus an antibiotic resistance gene. Everything else serves one of three jobs. The ends have to join, the right colony has to be findable, and the reading frame across the junction has to survive.”',
     '“And there is one idea that holds all the methods together. Every one of them answers the same question. How do I make two pieces of DNA carry ends that will find each other? They differ only in what makes those ends compatible.”'],
  note:'<b>第一段做三件事</b>：交代出处层（为什么是 DNA）、给定义、给形状。<br>⚠ <b>“marked absence of tools for targeted manipulation at the protein level” 是幻灯片原话，照用。</b>这是「为什么需要重组 DNA 技术」那道题的第二层，<b>大多数人只答第一层，而第二层才是考官在等的</b>。<span class="pg">L1 s.21</span><br>⚠ <b>第三句那条轴是我自己的整理</b>，被问出处就这么说。但笔记最后一节自己说答案是一个<b>选择</b>，所以它不是外挂上去的。'},
 {tag:'段 2 · general', h:'四族方法按「末端怎么来的」排开，一族两句',
  p:['“There are four answers and every method on the course is one of them. The first is a cut inside the recognition site. Type two P enzymes such as EcoRI and BamHI recognise a palindrome and cut within it, so the overhang sequence is dictated entirely by the enzyme, and T4 ligase closes it. That is classical restriction cloning.”',
     '“The second is a cut outside the recognition site. Type two S enzymes such as BsaI cut at a fixed distance from their site, so the four base overhang has a sequence I choose, and the site itself sits on the piece that is thrown away. That gives a scarless junction and directional assembly of many fragments in one tube. That is Golden Gate.”',
     '“The third is a chewed back single strand. LIC uses T4 DNA polymerase as an exonuclease, stopped at a designed position by supplying only one nucleotide, and Gibson uses T5 exonuclease with overlaps of twenty to forty base pairs. The overhangs are long enough to anneal on their own, so LIC needs no ligase at all and the cell repairs the nicks.”',
     '“The fourth is no cut at all. Gateway borrows the site specific recombination of phage lambda, so there is no restriction enzyme and no ligase anywhere in it. And there is a fifth case that shows the axis is the right one. In TA cloning the end comes from the polymerase rather than from any cutting enzyme, because Taq adds a single A to each end of the product.”'],
  note:'<b>这一段是这张卡的主承重段。</b>它同时回答「有哪些方法」和「它们凭什么是一类」，而且用的是同一个逻辑：<b>按末端的来处排，不按名字排。</b><br><b>每一族只说两句</b>：末端怎么来的，谁把它封上。<b>不要在这一段里报年份、公司名、效率数字</b>——那些留给追问，他问哪个你给哪个。<br>⚠ 他很可能在这一段中间打断，指着某一族问下去。<b>那正是这段的目的</b>：你把地图摊开，让他自己挑一格。'},
 {tag:'段 3 · 稍展开', h:'磷酸账，然后是「选 vs 筛」的三个陷阱',
  p:['“Underneath all of that there is one rule worth tracking. T4 ligase needs a five prime phosphate and a three prime hydroxyl, both present. Restriction enzymes leave a five prime phosphate, so cut vector and insert ligate directly. Synthetic oligonucleotides are made with a five prime hydroxyl, so a PCR product made with ordinary primers cannot be ligated at that end unless I phosphorylate it.”',
     '“The same rule is used deliberately on the vector. A vector cut with one enzyme can religate to itself, and empty self ligated vector transforms very efficiently, so it is the biggest source of background colonies. Dephosphorylating it makes that impossible. But if I did a directional double digest with two incompatible enzymes, the vector could not religate anyway, and dephosphorylating only costs me efficiency.”',
     '“Then I have to find the right colony, and I would separate selection from screening. Selection means the wrong cells do not survive, and that is the antibiotic, or ccdB counter selection where the unreacted vector kills its own host. Screening means the wrong cells are visible, and that is blue white screening or colony PCR.”',
     '“Two traps live there. A satellite colony is not a transformant, because secreted beta lactamase clears the ampicillin in a halo and plasmid free cells grow inside it. And a white colony only tells me the lacZ alpha fragment was disrupted. It says nothing about the orientation or the sequence, so I still confirm by colony PCR or sequencing.”'],
  note:'<b>这一段是「答八分」的典范</b>：它不给任何一种方法的细节，只给<b>贯穿所有方法的两件事</b>——磷酸账，和怎么知道成了。<br><b>选 vs 筛这个区分要说出口</b>：不说的话，蓝白斑听起来就像一种选择，而它不是。<b>「把筛当成选」正是这一组三个陷阱的共同形状。</b><br>⚠ <b>「记账不是化学」是我自己的说法</b>，意思是磷酸酶没改变连接的化学，只是把一边的账目抹掉。说的时候可以直接用这句中文的意思，但别挂到讲义上。'},
 {tag:'段 4 · 留口子', h:'落到她自己在做的那一步：建一个展示文库，就是同一个克隆问题放大了',
  p:['“The place this touches my own work is building a display library. A library is not one clone. It is very many, so the joining step stops being a step in a protocol and becomes the thing that decides how large the library is.”',
     '“That changes which method makes sense. The insert has to sit in frame between the surface anchor and the tags, so the junction has to be scarless and Gateway is ruled out by its eight residue scar. The same parts come back every round, so a one pot method with designed overhangs pays for its domestication cost.”',
     '“It also changes how the DNA goes in. An assembly or a ligation product is exactly the case where the number of successful events is already small, so this is where electroporation stops being a preference and becomes a requirement. Chemical transformation is fine for moving an existing plasmid around.”',
     '“And I would finish with the answer the lecture itself gives, because I think it is the honest one. The technical rule gives me a shortlist. But in a real lab you use the system already implemented there. That is where the optimised protocols are, that is where the know how is, and those are the reagents and the standard vectors you already have.”'],
  note:'<b>两个口子都在主场</b>：<b>文库和选择</b>接她自己的工作和卡 <b>land</b>（fitness landscape）；<b>电穿孔和转化效率</b>接卡 <b>14</b>；<b>质粒进去之后发生什么</b>接卡 <b>pe-expr</b>。<br><b>「A library is not one clone」这一句本身就很好</b>——它说明她知道克隆的效率在文库这件事上不是方便性问题，而是<b>文库大小本身</b>。<br>⚠ <b>不要在这里给文库大小的数字。</b>笔记里没有，编一个数是这场考试里最危险的动作（LOGIC 第 11 条）。要数就给判据：<b>成功事件的数目本来就少的时候，效率才要紧。</b><br>最后一句是<b>幻灯片自己的答案</b>，可以直接引，而且它把这道题从「背方法」变成「懂约束」。<span class="pg">L2 s.33</span>'}
],

why:{
 rungs:[
  ['为什么克隆方法有这么多种，一种不够吗？','因为它们在<b>三件事上互相取舍</b>：<b>接口干不干净 · 一次能拼几段 · 序列上有没有约束</b>。没有一种把三样全占了。经典酶切便宜、人人会，但接口留疤、还要求插入片段里没有同样的位点；Golden Gate 无疤又能多段，但要先 domestication；Gateway 效率最高又能一对多，但留八个残基；Gibson 什么约束都没有，但要设计 20–40 bp 的重叠还要测拼缝。<b>方法多，是因为约束多。</b>'],
  ['那为什么「末端怎么来的」比方法的名字更好用？','因为<b>末端的来处直接决定了其余全部性质</b>。切在位点<b>里面</b>→ 末端序列是酶的，所以只能拼一段、而且位点留在产物里；切在位点<b>外面</b>→ 末端序列是你的，所以能定向、能多段、而且位点被丢掉了所以无疤；<b>啃</b>出来的单链 → 长到不需要连接酶，长度和位置都是设计出来的；<b>不切</b> → 连「插入片段里不能有这个位点」这个前提都不需要，但重组位点必须留在产物里，<b>于是有疤</b>。<br><b>所以「有没有疤」不是每种方法各自的怪癖，它是「位点跑哪儿去了」的直接后果。</b>'],
  ['那 Golden Gate 一锅里又切又连，为什么不会自己拆自己？','因为<b>切和连不是同时对同一个接口起作用的</b>。接对了的接口<b>把识别位点毁掉了</b>——位点在被丢掉的那一小段上——所以酶再也认不出它；接错的、或者自己连回去的载体<b>把位点重新造了出来</b>，于是被再切一次，回到池子里。<b>每一轮切掉的都只是错的那些。</b>'],
  ['那为什么这个循环一定往对的方向走，而不是原地打转？','因为它不靠选择性，靠的是<b>错误可逆、正确不可逆</b>。对的产物是一个<b>出不来的陷阱态</b>，错的产物每一轮都被放回池子里重来。<b>20–40 个循环下来，池子只能往一个方向排空。</b>再往下问就是「一个不可逆的步骤怎么把整个平衡拉过去」——<b>那已经是热力学，不是克隆了。</b>']
 ],
 stop:{lbl:'停 · 落在热力学',
  say:'“Below that we are asking how an irreversible step pulls an entire equilibrium across, and that is thermodynamics rather than cloning.”'}
},

/* ---------------- 同一个答案，不同问法 ---------------- */
recog:[
{q:'How do you clone a gene?',
 mean:'<b>最短的问法，也是最可能的那一个。</b>答案要自带结构：<b>定义 → 那条轴 → 四个答案 → 停</b>。<b>不要报七个方法的名字。</b>',
 say:'“Cloning means joining a gene to a vector so the joined circle replicates inside a cell. Every method for doing it answers the same question. How do I make two pieces of DNA carry ends that will find each other? They differ only in what makes those ends compatible. There are four answers. A cut inside the recognition site, a cut outside it, a chewed back single strand, or a recombinase that needs no cut at all.”',
 tail:'<b>说完就停。</b>这是八分答案。他接下来挑哪一族，你就只讲那一族——<b>五种一起倒，等于自己把终点往前搬</b>（LOGIC 第 12 条）。'},

{q:'What makes Golden Gate scarless?',
 mean:'考的是<b>那一条定义性质</b>：Type IIS 切在<b>识别位点外面</b>。不说这一条，后面全是背的。',
 say:'“Because a type two S enzyme cuts outside its own recognition sequence. The site therefore ends up on the small piece that is discarded, so it is not present in the assembled product. The same fact gives me the second advantage. The enzyme does not dictate the four base overhang, so I design each junction myself, and four bases give two hundred and fifty six possibilities.”',
 tail:'<b>一条事实推出两个结论，这正是这道题想听的。</b>顺势可以给棘轮：接对了的接口毁掉了位点所以切不动，接错的重造了位点所以被再切一次，<b>20–40 个循环把反应推向全对</b>。⚠ 棘轮那段在 beyondPoints。'},

{q:'What does a white colony tell you?',
 mean:'⚠ <b>陷阱题。</b>他要的不是蓝白斑的机制，是<b>它不报告什么</b>。',
 say:'“It tells me the lacZ alpha fragment was disrupted, which means something was inserted into the cloning site. It does not tell me the insert went in the right way round and it does not tell me the sequence is correct. Both still have to be confirmed, by colony PCR or by sequencing. Cloning is not a hundred per cent efficient, so that confirmation step is never optional.”',
 tail:'<b>先答它证明了什么，再答它没证明什么</b>，顺序反了听起来像在找补。机制顺手带一句：<b>α 片段 59 个残基在质粒上，ω 片段在染色体上，互补之后 β-半乳糖苷酶切 X-gal 出蓝色不溶产物</b>。'},

{q:'Which cloning system would you use?',
 mean:'⚠ 他要的是<b>三个问题</b>，然后是<b>幻灯片自己的那句答案</b>。<b>只给决策表，答得不完整。</b>',
 say:'“I would ask three questions. Does the junction have to be clean, because if I need an authentic N terminus then Gateway is out. What shape is the assembly, because standardised parts mean Golden Gate and one gene into many vectors means Gateway. And is there a hard constraint, because if every enzyme in the cloning site also cuts inside my gene I go to Gibson or LIC. But the honest answer is that in a real lab you use the system already implemented there. That is where the protocols and the reagents and the standard vectors already are.”',
 tail:'<b>最后那句是幻灯片自己给的答案</b>，不是我加的谦虚话。<b>考官问这道题，一半是在看你知不知道约束既是技术上的也是现实上的。</b><span class="pg">L2 s.33</span>'},

{q:'Why do you dephosphorylate the vector, and when would you not?',
 mean:'考的是<b>那条磷酸规则的一次故意使用</b>。<b>第二半句比第一半句值钱。</b>',
 say:'“Because a vector cut with a single enzyme has two complementary ends and can religate to itself. Empty self ligated vector transforms very efficiently, so it is the single biggest source of background colonies. Removing its five prime phosphates makes self ligation impossible, because ligase needs a five prime phosphate on at least one side of each nick. The insert keeps its own phosphates, so the real junctions still form and the cell repairs the two nicks. I would not do it after a directional double digest with incompatible ends, because then the vector cannot religate anyway and the step only costs efficiency.”',
 tail:'<b>「定向克隆是同一个问题的更好解法」这句要说出来</b>，而且它多给你一样东西：<b>插入片段的方向被固定死了</b>。（不该做的那半在 beyondPoints。）'},

{q:'How does Gibson assembly work with three enzymes in one tube?',
 mean:'考的是<b>它们为什么不互相拆台</b>。答案是<b>热稳定性的差异</b>，不是加料顺序。',
 say:'“Everything happens at fifty degrees in one tube. T5 exonuclease chews back the five prime ends and exposes complementary single strands, and the designed overlaps of twenty to forty base pairs anneal. The key is that T5 exonuclease is heat labile, so it inactivates itself early in the incubation and cannot destroy the annealed product. Phusion then fills the gaps and the thermostable Taq ligase seals the nicks. The order in time comes from a difference in thermal stability rather than from adding things in steps.”',
 tail:'⚠ <b>连接酶是 Taq 不是 T4</b>，因为 T4 在 50 °C 会变性。<b>「顺序来自热稳定性的差异」这句是这条答案的分水岭。</b>（这段在 beyondPoints；幻灯片自己只给了「拼缝要测序」这条注意。）'},

{q:'Why does protein engineering need recombinant DNA technology at all?',
 mean:'笔记自己说这是<b>整门课的概念基石</b>。<b>答案有三层，大多数人只答第一层。</b>',
 say:'“Three layers. The central dogma says information never passes from protein to protein or from protein to nucleic acid, so a protein cannot be templated and cannot be amplified. There is no protein polymerase and no protein PCR. Second, there is a marked absence of tools for targeted manipulation at the protein level. Chemical methods exist but label every accessible lysine, and the specific enzymatic ones all need a genetically encoded tag, so they take you back to DNA anyway. Third, therefore the only way to make a specific change reproducibly and at scale is to make it in the DNA.”',
 tail:'<b>第二层是考官在等的那一层</b>，而 “marked absence of tools for targeted manipulation at the protein level” 是幻灯片原话。<b>翻译后修饰是宿主装的，不是你装的</b>——这也是为什么宿主选择占一整讲。<span class="pg">L1 s.21</span>'},

{q:'You need an authentic N-terminus. Which method is ruled out?',
 mean:'<b>一个关键词直接映射到一个方法。</b>他在测你有没有把「疤」当成真问题。',
 say:'“Gateway is ruled out. The attB sites remain in the final construct and they are translated, so about eight extra amino acids appear at the fusion junction. For routine expression that is harmless. It is not harmless when I need an authentic N terminus, or a crystal structure where extra flexible residues interfere. It is also not harmless for a signal peptide or a protease cleavage site, because there the added residues change the very sequence I am studying. I would use Golden Gate, Gibson, LIC or In-Fusion instead.”',
 tail:'<b>「不是脚注，是死穴」这个态度要传达出来。</b>笔记的原话是：题面一提 authentic 或 native N-terminus，<b>Gateway 就是要被排除的那一个</b>。（这条在 beyondPoints。）'},

{q:'Why can a eukaryotic gene not be expressed in E. coli straight from genomic DNA?', odd:1,
 mean:'听起来像分子生物学的常识题，笔记明说它是<b>经典口试题</b>。一句话答案。',
 say:'“Introns. Eukaryotic genomic DNA contains them and prokaryotes have no spliceosome, so the introns are transcribed and translated along with the exons and the product is nonsense. The way round it is RT-PCR. You start from mature spliced messenger RNA and reverse transcribe it into cDNA, and that cDNA is intron free by construction rather than by luck, because the cell did the splicing before I touched it.”',
 tail:'<b>先给一个词，再给理由。</b>这道题的答案就是 introns，说完再展开。<span class="pg">L1 s.24</span>'},

{q:'There are hundreds of tiny colonies around the big ones. What are they?', odd:1,
 mean:'听起来是操作问题，考的是<b>抗性机制</b>。<b>它们不是转化子。</b>',
 say:'“Those are satellite colonies and they are not transformants. Ampicillin resistance works by beta lactamase, and that enzyme is secreted into the periplasm and leaks into the medium, so it destroys the ampicillin in a halo around each resistant colony. Plasmid free cells then grow inside that cleared zone. Picking one gives me no plasmid at all. The fixes are carbenicillin, which resists the enzyme better, or simply not over incubating the plate and picking only well isolated colonies.”',
 tail:'<b>顺势给对比</b>：<b>卡那霉素没有这个问题</b>，因为它的抗性酶在细胞里修饰药物，而不是把培养基里的药整批清掉。<b>这是 pET 多用卡那的实在理由。</b>（这一条在 beyondPoints。）'},

{q:'Your digest did not cut, but the plasmid map says the site is there. What happened?', odd:1,
 mean:'考的是<b>甲基化</b>。危险就在于<b>图看上去完全正常</b>。',
 say:'“The most likely cause is methylation. Standard cloning strains such as DH5 alpha and TOP10 are Dam positive and Dcm positive, so plasmid prepared from them carries those methyl marks. Enzymes like XbaI, ClaI and MboI are blocked when their site overlaps a GATC. The map cannot show that, because a map does not know whether my DNA was methylated. The fix is to propagate the plasmid in a dam minus dcm minus strain and then digest.”',
 tail:'<b>排查顺序也要能报</b>：<b>甲基化 → 切得离末端太近（缺填充碱基）→ 缓冲液盐浓度或星号活性</b>。<b>甲基化排第一，正因为它最隐蔽。</b>（这条在 beyondPoints。）'},

{q:'Why would a protein be made, secreted, and still impossible to purify?', odd:1,
 mean:'听起来像纯化题，其实是<b>设计题的那个终止密码子陷阱</b>。',
 say:'“Because a stop codon was created at the junction, in front of the tag. In the worked exercise the spacer before the EcoRV site could be TA, and read across the junction that spells TAG, an amber stop codon. Translation terminates before the myc and histidine tag, so the protein is made and secreted perfectly well and there is simply no tag on it. The lesson is that a spacer has to be checked together with the sequence on either side of it, not on its own.”',
 tail:'<b>顺手给一句把整门课串起来的话</b>：<b>TAG 正是第 7、8 讲里被重新指派去掺入非天然氨基酸的那个密码子</b>。这里它是毁掉构建体的 bug，那里它是整个功能。<span class="pg">L2 s.35–43</span>'},

{q:'Why does a cloning plasmid carry more copies than an expression plasmid?', odd:1,
 mean:'反直觉的那一条。答案是<b>代谢负担</b>，而且要先说<b>是 ORI 定的</b>。',
 say:'“Copy number is set by the origin of replication. A cloning plasmid exists only to give yield, so higher is strictly better, and pUC sits at five hundred to seven hundred copies. An expression plasmid is different. Too high a copy number is a metabolic burden, because the cell spends its resources replicating plasmid and transcribing the foreign gene instead of growing. It grows badly, expresses less, or loses the plasmid. The vector pET uses the pBR322 origin and has only fifteen to twenty copies.”',
 tail:'<b>学生通常以为表达载体是高拷贝的。</b>笔记专门把这条列成一个 surprise。（解释在 beyondPoints，两个数字在幻灯片上。）'},

{q:'Why can you not just put a ligase-ready end on your PCR primer?', odd:1,
 mean:'考的是<b>磷酸账</b>。听起来像抱怨，答案是一条化学事实。',
 say:'“Because synthetic oligonucleotides are made with a five prime hydroxyl rather than a five prime phosphate, and T4 ligase needs a five prime phosphate and a three prime hydroxyl, both present. So a PCR product amplified with ordinary primers cannot be ligated at that end at all. There are two fixes. Order five prime phosphorylated primers, or treat the product with T4 polynucleotide kinase, which transfers a phosphate from ATP onto the five prime hydroxyl.”',
 tail:'<b>对比一句</b>：<b>限制酶留下的末端自带 5′-磷酸</b>，所以刚切的载体和插入片段可以直接连，不用任何额外处理。<b>同一条规则解释了两件看着无关的事。</b>'},

{q:'Why would you pay eighty dollars for a plasmid you could make yourself?', odd:1,
 mean:'听起来像预算问题，考的是<b>第一条路：先问这一步能不能不做</b>。',
 say:'“Because the cheapest route is almost always that somebody has already done it. In principle the authors of a paper are obliged to send you the clone, since material sharing is a condition of publishing in most journals. Addgene holds about a hundred thousand reagents, and there you mostly pay shipping, roughly eighty dollars. What that buys is not the DNA. It is the cloning, the sequencing, the host optimisation and the purification development that somebody already did once.”',
 tail:'<b>「买的不是 DNA，是别人已经做过一遍的那几个月」这句话本身就很好。</b><span class="pg">L1 s.22–23</span>'}
],

/* ---------------- 追问 ---------------- */
ask:[
{g:'定义类', gn:'这张卡的英文句里用到的词，他会一个个拎出来问。<b>这一科是新的，所以定义链要给得比生化那边更满。</b>', items:[
{r:'高', q:'What is a vector, and what is the minimal plasmid?',
    ez:'“A vector is a D N A molecule that carries a passenger sequence. It also replicates on its own inside a host. A plasmid is the usual one. It is a small circular D N A molecule. It replicates independently of the chromosome. It is typically fifteen hundred to twenty thousand base pairs. The minimal viable plasmid needs two things. It needs an origin of replication. It needs an antibiotic resistance gene. Nothing else is strictly required. Everything beyond that was added for a purpose I can name.”',
    ezcn:'<b>载体 ＝ 一个 DNA 分子，它带着搭车的序列，并且能在宿主里自己复制。</b><b>常用的是质粒</b>：<b>小的环状 DNA，独立于染色体复制</b>，一般 <b>1500–20000 bp</b>。<b>最小可用质粒只要两样：一个复制起点 ＋ 一个抗性基因</b>，<b>别的都不是必需的</b>。<b>其余每一样都是为了某个我能说出名字的目的加上去的。</b>',
 en:'“A vector is a DNA molecule that carries a passenger sequence and replicates on its own inside a host. A plasmid is the usual one, a small circular DNA molecule replicating independently of the chromosome, typically fifteen hundred to twenty thousand base pairs. The minimal viable plasmid is an origin of replication plus an antibiotic resistance gene, and nothing else is strictly required. Everything beyond that is added for a purpose I can name.”',
 cn:'<b>这是这张卡的第一个承重词</b>，不交代它，「克隆」就只是一个动作名。<span class="pg">L2 s.4–6</span><br><b>「最小质粒」这个说法很好用</b>：它把质粒图上一堆元件变成「在这两个之外，每一个都是为某件事加的」。'},
{r:'高', q:'What is an origin of replication, and what does it decide?',
    ez:'“It is the position where replication of the plasmid begins. It is rich in A and T. So it has a lower melting temperature. The strands separate there more easily. Host proteins carry out the replication. The plasmid does not encode its own replisome. The origin decides two things. It decides the copy number, which is delicately balanced. And it decides compatibility. Two plasmids sharing an origin compete for the same machinery. So they cannot be stably kept in one cell.”',
    ezcn:'<b>复制起点 ＝ 质粒开始复制的那个位置。</b>它<b>富含 A 和 T</b>，<b>所以解链温度低，链在那里更容易分开</b>。<b>复制由宿主的蛋白完成，质粒自己不编码复制体</b>。<b>它决定两件事</b>：<b>拷贝数</b>（这个平衡很精细），以及<b>相容性</b>——<b>两个共用同一起点的质粒会争同一套机器，没法稳定地待在同一个细胞里。</b>',
 en:'“It is the position where replication of the plasmid begins. It is rich in A and T, so it has a lower melting temperature and the strands separate more easily. The replication itself is carried out by host proteins, because the plasmid does not encode its own replisome. What it decides is the copy number, which is delicately balanced. It also decides compatibility, because two plasmids sharing an origin compete for the same machinery and cannot be stably kept in one cell.”',
 cn:'<b>三件事要一次给全</b>：起点在哪、拷贝数、相容性。<span class="pg">L2 s.4–6</span><br><b>「复制是宿主蛋白干的」这半句容易漏</b>，但它解释了为什么同 ORI 会竞争——<b>竞争的是宿主的那套机器。</b>共表达那一半在卡 <b>pe-expr</b>。'},
{r:'高', q:'What is the difference between a type two P and a type two S restriction enzyme?',
    ez:'“Type two P enzymes recognise a palindromic sequence. They cut inside it. So the overhang is blunt or sticky. Its sequence is dictated entirely by the enzyme. EcoRI, BamHI and HindIII are examples. They are about ninety per cent of what gets used. Type two S enzymes recognise a non palindromic sequence. They cut outside it, at a fixed distance. BsaI, BbsI and BsmBI are the examples. That one property is what makes Golden Gate possible.”',
    ezcn:'<b>Ⅱ-P 型认回文序列，在序列内部切</b>，<b>所以末端（平或粘）的序列完全由酶说了算</b>（EcoRI、BamHI、HindIII、NotI，<b>占实际使用的九成</b>）。<b>Ⅱ-S 型认非回文序列，在序列外面固定距离处切</b>（BsaI、BbsI、BsmBI）。<b>就这一条性质，成全了 Golden Gate。</b>',
 en:'“Type two P enzymes recognise a palindromic sequence and cut inside it, so the overhang is blunt or sticky with a sequence dictated entirely by the enzyme. EcoRI, BamHI, HindIII and NotI are examples, and they are about ninety per cent of what gets used. Type two S enzymes recognise a non palindromic sequence and cut outside it, at a fixed distance. BsaI, BbsI and BsmBI are the examples, and that one property is what makes Golden Gate possible.”',
 cn:'<b>这一条是这张卡最值得背熟的一句。</b><span class="pg">L2 s.9–10</span><br><b>说完立刻给两个后果</b>：位点不进产物（无疤痕），末端序列由你定（可定向多段）。<b>只说「切在外面」而不说后果，等于只说了一半。</b>'},
{r:'高', q:'What does positive selection mean, and what does negative selection mean?',
    ez:'“Positive selection means only the cells I want survive. Antibiotic resistance is the example. No plasmid means no resistance gene. So the cell dies on the antibiotic. Negative selection means the cells I do not want are actively killed. It is also called counter selection. The ccdB toxin is the example. An unreacted destination vector still carries ccdB. It carries it in the slot my gene should occupy. So it poisons its own host. Only vectors where the gene replaced ccdB survive.”',
    ezcn:'<b>正选择 ＝ 只有我想要的细胞活得下来</b>（例子是<b>抗生素抗性</b>：没质粒就没抗性基因，<b>上了抗生素就死</b>）。<b>负选择／反选择 ＝ 我不想要的细胞被主动杀掉</b>（例子是 <b>ccdB 毒素</b>：<b>没反应的目的载体，我的基因该占的那个位置上还坐着 ccdB，于是它毒死自己的宿主</b>；<b>只有基因把 ccdB 换掉的那些活下来</b>）。',
 en:'“Positive selection means only the cells I want survive. Antibiotic resistance is the example, because no plasmid means no resistance gene and the cell dies on the antibiotic. Negative or counter selection means the cells I do not want are actively killed. The ccdB toxin is the example, because the unreacted destination vector still carries ccdB in the slot my gene should occupy, so it poisons its own host. Only vectors where the gene replaced ccdB survive.”',
 cn:'<b>这一对要说得干脆</b>，因为 Gateway 的 >95% 就是<b>两层一起用</b>的结果。<span class="pg">L2 s.8</span><br>⚠ <b>筛选（screening）是第三件事，不要跟这两个混</b>：蓝白斑和菌落 PCR <b>不杀任何东西</b>，它们只是让错的<b>看得出来</b>。'},
{r:'高', q:'What is ccdB and what does it inhibit?',
    ez:'“CcdB is the toxin half of a toxin antitoxin system. That system is encoded by the ccd operon of the E. coli F plasmid. CcdA is the antitoxin. It dissociates the toxin from its target. CcdB inhibits D N A gyrase. Gyrase is the bacterial type two topoisomerase. It cuts both strands of the helix to relax supercoiling. It is indispensable for survival. That is also why the human version is a chemotherapy target.”',
    ezcn:'<b>ccdB 是一个毒素–抗毒素系统里的毒素那一半</b>，来自<b>大肠杆菌 F 质粒的 ccd 操纵子</b>；<b>ccdA 是抗毒素</b>，<b>把毒素从它的靶子上拆下来</b>。<b>ccdB 抑制的是 DNA 旋转酶（gyrase）</b>，<b>细菌的 Ⅱ 型拓扑异构酶</b>——<b>它切断双链来松开超螺旋，对生存不可或缺</b>。<b>人的对应物是化疗药的靶点，同一个道理。</b>',
 en:'“CcdB is the toxin half of a toxin antitoxin system encoded by the ccd operon of the E. coli F plasmid. CcdA is the antitoxin, and it dissociates the toxin from its target. CcdB inhibits DNA gyrase, the bacterial type two topoisomerase. That enzyme cuts both strands of the helix to relax supercoiling and is indispensable for survival, which is also why the human version is a chemotherapy target.”',
 cn:'<b>把「为什么抑制它就致死」说出来</b>，比只说「它是毒素」强。<span class="pg">L2 s.8</span><br>⚠ 连带的一条：<b>带 ccdB 的目的载体要在 DB3.1 或 ccdB Survival 里扩</b>，那里的旋转酶是突变过的。JM109、XL1-Blue、XL10-Gold 天然带 F 质粒，所以<b>部分</b>耐受。'},
{r:'中', q:'What is domestication in Golden Gate?',
 en:'“Domestication means removing every internal site for the assembly enzyme from a part before you use it. Any internal BsaI or BbsI or BsmBI site would be cut during the reaction and fragment the part, giving truncated assemblies. You remove them with silent mutations, changing the codon and keeping the amino acid, which is only possible because the genetic code is degenerate. It is a one time cost per part, and afterwards the part is reusable for ever.”',
 cn:'<b>「一次性成本，永久收益」这个说法是这条答案的重点</b>——它解释了为什么会有 MoClo、GoldenBraid 2.0、Mobius Assembly、EMMA 这些标准件库。<span class="pg">L2 s.20–21</span><br>⚠ <b>沉默突变之所以做得成，跟密码子优化是同一个理由：遗传密码简并。</b>（domestication 的细节在 beyondPoints。）'},
{r:'中', q:'What is an exonuclease, and what is an endonuclease?',
 en:'“An endonuclease cuts within a nucleic acid chain, and an exonuclease removes nucleotides from an end. Endonucleases split into specific ones, which are the restriction enzymes plus phage lambda integrase and excisionase, and non specific ones such as RNase H and DNase one. Exonucleases can run five prime to three prime or the other way, and the category includes the proofreading activity of DNA polymerases. T5 exonuclease is the chew back enzyme in Gibson assembly.”',
 cn:'<b>一句话记法：内切从中间切，外切从末端啃。</b><span class="pg">L1 s.28</span><br><b>这一节看着像目录，其实是在给每一种克隆方法发零件</b>：<b>λ 整合酶和切除酶就是 Gateway 卖的东西，T5 外切酶就是 Gibson 的引擎。</b><b>反应类型本身接卡 x-rxn。</b>'},
{r:'中', q:'What is RNase H, and why is it interesting?',
 en:'“RNase H hydrolyses the phosphodiester bonds of RNA, but only when that RNA is hybridised to DNA. It leaves free RNA alone and it does not digest DNA at all, single stranded or double stranded. That specificity is what makes it useful, because after reverse transcription the product is an RNA DNA hybrid, and RNase H removes the RNA strand without touching the cDNA.”',
 cn:'<b>「只认杂合体」是这条的全部</b>。<span class="pg">L1 s.28</span><br>对比一句：<b>DNase I 双链单链 DNA 都降</b>，<b>微球菌核酸酶</b>连 RNA 一起降，而且留下带 3′-磷酸的寡核苷酸。<b>逆转录酶本身接卡 taq。</b>'},
{r:'中', q:'What is alpha complementation?',
 en:'“Beta galactosidase needs to tetramerise to be active, and tetramerisation is mediated by the N terminal part of the protein. That is what makes splitting it possible. The large omega fragment is encoded on the bacterial chromosome and the small alpha fragment of fifty nine residues is carried on the plasmid, with the cloning site inside it. When both are present they complement and active enzyme forms, and an insert in the cloning site destroys the alpha fragment so no enzyme forms.”',
 cn:'<b>先说为什么这个酶能被劈开</b>，再说劈成了哪两半。这样蓝白斑就不是一个要背的事实了。<span class="pg">L2 s.16–17</span><br><b>lacZ、lac 启动子、IPTG 那一整套在卡 12。</b>'}
]},

{g:'四族分开问', gn:'他可以指着任何一族问下去。<b>每一族只答两句：末端是怎么来的，谁把它封上。</b>细节挂在这两句下面。', items:[
{r:'高', q:'Walk me through classical restriction cloning.',
    ez:'“There are seven steps. Amplify the gene by P C R. Put restriction sites in the primer tails. Cut the insert. Cut the plasmid with complementary enzymes. Dephosphorylate the plasmid if needed. Ligate with T four ligase. That runs overnight at sixteen degrees, or ten minutes at room temperature. Transform. Then select the positive colonies. Two design points sit in the primer tails. Add stuffer bases outside the site, because enzymes cut poorly at the very end. And keep the reading frame if I am making a fusion.”',
    ezcn:'<b>七步。</b><b>①</b> PCR 扩增基因，<b>把酶切位点放在引物尾巴上</b>；<b>②</b> 切插入片段；<b>③</b> 用互补的酶切质粒；<b>④</b>（可选）把质粒<b>去磷酸化</b>；<b>⑤</b> 用 <b>T4 连接酶</b>连（<b>16 ℃ 过夜，或室温 10 分钟</b>）；<b>⑥</b> 转化；<b>⑦</b> 挑阳性菌落。<b>两个设计要点都在引物尾巴上</b>：<b>位点外面要留填充碱基</b>（<b>酶在线性片段的最末端切不动</b>），<b>做融合蛋白时要保住读码框</b>。',
 en:'“Seven steps. Amplify the gene by PCR with restriction sites in the primer tails. Cut the insert. Cut the plasmid with complementary enzymes. Optionally dephosphorylate the plasmid. Ligate with T4 ligase, either overnight at sixteen degrees or ten minutes at room temperature. Transform. Select the positive colonies. Two design points sit in the primer tails. Add stuffer bases outside the site, because enzymes cut poorly at the very end of a linear fragment. And keep the reading frame if I am making a fusion.”',
 cn:'<span class="pg">L2 s.15</span>。<b>七步要能一口气报完</b>，因为它是后面所有方法的参照系——<b>每一种新方法都是在拿掉这七步里的某一步。</b><br>TA 拿掉了酶切；LIC 拿掉了连接酶；Gateway 两样都拿掉了；Gibson 把三步压进一管。'},
{r:'高', q:'Why does Golden Gate work in one tube when the enzyme and the ligase are working against each other?',
    ez:'“Because the two reactions do not act on the same junction. Digestion and ligation run at the same time. The tube cycles between about thirty seven degrees and sixteen degrees. Thirty seven is for cutting and sixteen is for ligating. A correctly assembled junction has destroyed the recognition site. The enzyme cuts outside the site. That outside piece was discarded. So the product cannot be cut again. It is trapped. An incorrect junction regenerates the site. It is cut again and returns to the pool. Over twenty to forty cycles the reaction is driven to the correct assembly.”',
    ezcn:'因为<b>这两个反应作用的不是同一个接缝</b>。<b>酶切和连接同时进行</b>，管子在 <b>37 ℃（切）和 16 ℃（连）</b>之间循环。<b>接对了的接缝，识别位点已经被销毁了</b>——<b>酶在位点外面切，而位点所在那一小块被扔掉了</b>，<b>所以产物切不动了，被锁住</b>。<b>接错了的接缝会把识别位点重新造出来，于是被再切开，回到池子里</b>。<b>跑二三十到四十轮，反应就被推向完全正确的组装。</b>',
 en:'“Because the two reactions do not act on the same junction. Digestion and ligation run at the same time, cycling between about thirty seven degrees to cut and sixteen degrees to ligate. A correctly assembled junction has destroyed the recognition site, because the enzyme cuts outside it and that outside piece was discarded, so the product cannot be cut again and it is trapped. An incorrect junction regenerates the site, is cut again and returns to the pool. Over twenty to forty cycles the reaction is driven to the fully correct assembly.”',
 cn:'<b>「错的可逆、对的不可逆」是这条的全部</b>，而且它是整张卡里最漂亮的机制。效率对 <b>5–10 个片段</b>也常在 <b>90% 以上</b>。<br>⚠ <b>棘轮这段在 beyondPoints</b>，幻灯片只写了「一锅、无疤、便宜、快」。说的时候标一下出处。'},
{r:'高', q:'How are the LIC overhangs made, if nothing is cutting?',
    ez:'“By stalling an exonuclease at a designed position. T four D N A polymerase has two activities. One is polymerase, which needs template and primer and nucleotides. The other is a strong three prime to five prime exonuclease. That one is template independent. Which activity dominates depends on the nucleotides in the tube. The L I C tails are designed to lack one base. Say they contain no G. You then incubate with T four polymerase and only d G T P. The exonuclease chews back. It reaches the first G it would have to remove. The polymerase immediately re adds it. So the enzyme stalls exactly there.”',
    ezcn:'<b>靠让外切酶停在设计好的位置上。</b><b>T4 DNA 聚合酶有两个活性</b>：<b>聚合</b>（要模板、引物、核苷酸）和<b>很强的 3′→5′ 外切</b>（<b>不需要模板</b>）。<b>哪个占上风，取决于管子里有哪些核苷酸</b>。<b>LIC 的尾巴被设计成缺一种碱基</b>（比如<b>不含 G</b>），<b>然后只加 dGTP 和 T4 聚合酶</b>：<b>外切酶往回啃，啃到第一个 G 时，聚合酶立刻又把它接回去，于是酶就卡在那儿了。</b>',
 en:'“By stalling an exonuclease at a designed position. T4 DNA polymerase has a polymerase activity that needs template and primer and nucleotides, and a strong template independent three prime to five prime exonuclease. Which one dominates depends on what nucleotides are in the tube. The LIC tails are designed to lack one base, say no G, and you incubate with T4 polymerase and only dGTP. The exonuclease chews back until it reaches the first G it would have to remove, the polymerase immediately re adds it, and the enzyme stalls there.”',
 cn:'<b>「末端的位置是被设计出来的，不是被切出来的」这句值得说。</b>结果是一个精确定义的、约 <b>15 个核苷酸</b>的 5′ 单链末端。<span class="pg">L2 s.29–30</span><br>⚠ 这段在 <b>beyondPoints</b>。<b>代价也要主动给：尾巴序列必须整段缺一种碱基，Gibson 没有这个限制。</b>'},
{r:'高', q:'Where does Gateway get its efficiency from?',
    ez:'“From two independent filters acting at once. The entry clone and the destination vector carry different resistance genes. So plating on the destination antibiotic already removes anything unreacted. And the destination vector carries ccdB. It carries it in the slot my gene will occupy. Any vector that did not recombine still expresses the toxin. It then kills its own host. Only vectors where recombination replaced ccdB with my gene survive. That double filter is what takes it above ninety five per cent.”',
    ezcn:'<b>靠两道互相独立、同时生效的筛子。</b><b>①</b> 入门克隆和目的载体<b>带的是不同的抗性基因</b>，<b>所以铺在目的载体的抗生素上，没反应的就已经被去掉了</b>；<b>②</b> 目的载体<b>在我基因该占的那个位置上装着 ccdB</b>，<b>没重组成的载体照样表达毒素，把自己的宿主杀了</b>。<b>只有「重组把 ccdB 换成我的基因」的那些活下来——这道双重筛子把效率推到 95% 以上。</b>',
 en:'“From two independent filters acting at once. The entry clone and the destination vector carry different antibiotic resistance genes, so plating on the destination antibiotic already removes anything unreacted. And the destination vector carries ccdB in the slot my gene will occupy, so any vector that did not recombine still expresses the toxin and kills its own host. Only vectors where recombination replaced ccdB with my gene survive. That double filter is what takes it above ninety five per cent.”',
 cn:'<b>「两个独立的筛子」这个说法比背 95% 这个数强得多。</b><span class="pg">L2 s.22–25</span><br>⚠ 这也是<b>正选择加负选择</b>同时用的唯一例子。（双重选择怎么给出 95% 这段在 beyondPoints。）'},
{r:'中', q:'Where does TOPO TA get the energy to ligate without a ligase?',
 en:'“From the bond it already broke. Vaccinia topoisomerase one cleaves at its recognition sequence and forms a covalent phosphotyrosyl bond between its own active site tyrosine and the three prime phosphate of the DNA. The energy of the cleaved phosphodiester bond is stored in that protein DNA linkage instead of being lost. When the five prime hydroxyl of the insert attacks, the enzyme releases itself and the bond re forms. No ATP and no ligase are needed, which is why it takes five minutes at room temperature.”',
 cn:'<b>这是这张卡上最漂亮的化学</b>，而且它直接解释了那个「五分钟」的数。<span class="pg">L2 s.26–28</span><br>⚠ 这段在 <b>beyondPoints</b>，幻灯片只说了酶已经共价结合在载体上、反应五分钟。<b>磷酸二酯键本身接卡 03 和 x-bonds。</b>'}
]},

{g:'最容易混的几对', gn:'乱，通常不是不知道，是两个东西挨得太近。<b>每一对都给一句能当场分开它们的判据。</b>', items:[
{r:'高', q:'Gibson and LIC both chew back a strand. What is the real difference?',
    ez:'“The enzymes and the constraint. L I C uses T four D N A polymerase in exonuclease mode. Its overlaps are twelve to eighteen base pairs. It needs separate reactions for vector and insert. It runs at room temperature. It typically joins two fragments. Gibson uses T five exonuclease with Phusion and Taq ligase. Its overlaps are twenty to forty base pairs. It is one tube and isothermal at fifty degrees. Five or six fragments are routine. Both are scarless. The headline difference is a constraint. The L I C tails must lack one of the four bases. Gibson imposes no sequence constraint at all.”',
    ezcn:'<b>差在酶和约束条件上。</b><b>LIC</b>：T4 DNA 聚合酶走外切模式，<b>重叠 12–18 bp</b>，<b>载体和插入要分开反应</b>，<b>室温</b>，<b>一般接两个片段</b>。<b>Gibson</b>：T5 外切酶 ＋ Phusion ＋ Taq 连接酶，<b>重叠 20–40 bp</b>，<b>一管、50 ℃ 恒温</b>，<b>五六个片段是常规</b>。<b>两个都无疤。</b><b>最要紧的差别是约束：LIC 的尾巴必须缺四种碱基里的一种，Gibson 对序列没有任何约束。</b>',
 en:'“The enzymes and the constraint. LIC uses T4 DNA polymerase in exonuclease mode with overlaps of twelve to eighteen base pairs, needs separate reactions for vector and insert, runs at room temperature and typically joins two fragments. Gibson uses T5 exonuclease with Phusion and Taq ligase, overlaps of twenty to forty base pairs, one tube, isothermal at fifty degrees, and five or six fragments routinely. Both are scarless. The headline difference is that the LIC tails must lack one of the four bases and Gibson imposes no sequence constraint at all.”',
 cn:'<b>判据一句话：谁在限制你的序列。</b>LIC 限制、Gibson 不限制——<b>这就是 Gibson 基本取代 LIC 的原因</b>，也是它能拼合成基因组的原因。<span class="pg">L2 s.29–32</span><br>⚠ 这张对照表在 <b>beyondPoints</b>。'},
{r:'高', q:'Selection and screening sound like the same thing. Are they?',
    ez:'“No. Selection means the cells I do not want cannot survive at all. The antibiotic is one example. The ccdB counter selection is another. There the unreacted vector kills its own host. Screening means every cell survives. I then have to look at them. Blue white screening is an example. So are colony P C R and sequencing. The practical consequence differs. Selection reduces the number of colonies on the plate. Screening reduces nothing. It only tells me which ones to pick.”',
    ezcn:'<b>不是。</b><b>选择 selection ＝ 我不想要的细胞根本活不下来</b>（抗生素；或者 ccdB 反选择——没反应的载体<b>把自己的宿主杀了</b>）。<b>筛选 screening ＝ 所有细胞都活着，我得一个一个去看</b>（蓝白斑、菌落 PCR、测序）。<b>实际后果完全不同：选择会减少平板上的菌落数；筛选一个也不减，它只告诉我该挑哪几个。</b>',
 en:'“No. Selection means the cells I do not want cannot survive at all, which is the antibiotic, or ccdB counter selection where the unreacted vector kills its own host. Screening means every cell survives and I have to look at them, which is blue white screening or colony PCR or sequencing. The practical consequence is different. Selection reduces the number of colonies on the plate. Screening does not reduce anything, it only tells me which ones to pick.”',
 cn:'<b>这一对是整个第五组的形状。</b>把筛当成选，就是蓝白斑那个陷阱的根源——<b>白色不是一道闸门，它只是一个提示。</b><br>⚠ <b>笔记没有把这两个并排比过，这是我按它给的定义推出来的</b>，说的时候别挂到讲义上。'},
{r:'高', q:'Is a scar the same thing as being out of frame?',
    ez:'“No, and the difference matters. A scar is extra sequence that stays in the construct. Gateway leaves about eight residues at the junction. Those are in frame by design. Being out of frame is different. The downstream sequence is read in the wrong triplets. So the tag or the leader becomes nonsense. A scarred construct still works for most purposes. An out of frame one produces nothing useful at all.”',
    ezcn:'<b>不是，而且这个区别很要紧。</b><b>疤 scar ＝ 留在构建里的多余序列</b>（Gateway 在接缝处留下<b>约八个残基</b>），<b>它是按设计在框内的</b>。<b>移码 out of frame ＝ 下游序列被按错误的三联体读</b>，<b>标签或前导序列变成乱码</b>。<b>带疤的构建大多数用途照样能用；移码的构建什么有用的东西都做不出来。</b>',
 en:'“No, and the difference matters. A scar is extra sequence that stays in the construct, like the eight residues Gateway leaves at the junction, and it is in frame by design. Being out of frame means the downstream sequence is read in the wrong triplets, so the tag or the leader is nonsense. A scarred construct still works for most purposes. An out of frame one produces nothing useful at all.”',
 cn:'<b>判据一句话：疤是「多了几个残基」，移框是「后面全废了」。</b><br>这一对值得准备，因为设计题里<b>两个问题挨在一起</b>：选哪个 pSecTag2 版本管的是框，选哪种克隆方法管的是疤。<b>笔记没把这两个并排讲，是我推的。</b>'},
{r:'中', q:'Ampicillin and kanamycin both select transformants. Why does only one give satellite colonies?',
 en:'“Because of where the resistance enzyme works. Beta lactamase is secreted into the periplasm and leaks into the medium, so it destroys ampicillin in a halo around each colony and plasmid free cells grow there. The kanamycin resistance enzyme is an intracellular phosphotransferase that modifies the drug inside the cell, so it never clears the drug from the agar. That is one practical reason kanamycin marked vectors like most pET plasmids are popular.”',
 cn:'<b>判据一句话：酶在哪里工作。</b>分泌出去的会改变培养基，留在里面的不会。<span class="pg">L2 s.7–8</span><br>⚠ 卫星菌落和卡那的对比都在 <b>beyondPoints</b>。'},
{r:'中', q:'Codon optimisation and domestication both change the DNA without changing the protein. Are they the same trick?',
 en:'“They use the same fact and they solve different problems. Both rely on the genetic code being degenerate, so a codon can be swapped for a synonymous one and the protein is unchanged. Codon optimisation swaps rare codons for abundant ones so the ribosome does not stall on scarce transfer RNAs. Domestication removes internal recognition sites for the assembly enzyme so the part is not cut during the reaction. One is about translation and the other is about the cloning chemistry.”',
 cn:'<b>这一对很值得准备</b>，因为它把两节之间的联系说穿了：<b>简并性是一个可以反复花的预算</b>。<span class="pg">L1 s.25–26 · L2 s.20–21</span><br>⚠ 「同一个花招用在两处」这个说法是我自己的。'}
]},

{g:'陷阱类', gn:'<b>这一组是分数所在。</b>每一条都是「纸上看着完全正确、台面上一定失败」的那种错，而且他很可能用故事的形式问出来。', items:[
{r:'高', q:'A student picks a white colony, sequences it, and the insert is backwards. What went wrong?',
    ez:'“Nothing went wrong with the screening. A white colony reports one thing only. The lacZ alpha fragment was disrupted. So something was inserted. It reports nothing about orientation. It reports nothing about sequence either. If the cloning was not directional, both orientations are equally likely. A T A cloning or a single enzyme digest is not directional. So half the white colonies are backwards. Prevent it with directional cloning, using two incompatible enzymes. Catch it with colony P C R or sequencing.”',
    ezcn:'<b>筛选本身没出错。</b><b>白斑只报告一件事：lacZ α 片段被破坏了，也就是「有东西插进去了」</b>，<b>它不报告方向，也不报告序列</b>。<b>如果这次克隆不是定向的</b>（比如 <b>TA 克隆</b>或者<b>只用一个酶切</b>），<b>两个方向的概率一样，所以一半白斑是反的</b>。<b>预防靠定向克隆——用两个不相容的酶；发现靠菌落 PCR 或测序。</b>',
 en:'“Nothing went wrong with the screening. A white colony only reports that the lacZ alpha fragment was disrupted, which means something was inserted. It reports nothing about orientation or sequence. If the cloning was not directional, for example a TA cloning or a single enzyme digest, then both orientations are equally likely and half the white colonies are backwards. The way to prevent it is directional cloning with two incompatible enzymes, and the way to catch it is colony PCR or sequencing.”',
 cn:'<b>「筛选没有出错」这个开头很好</b>——它说明你知道这个方法的边界，而不是以为方法失灵了。<span class="pg">L2 s.16–17</span><br><b>预防和发现是两件事，两个都要给。</b>（白色不证明什么这条在 beyondPoints。）'},
{r:'高', q:'You designed the primer with the restriction site right at the end. Why will that fail?',
    ez:'“Because restriction enzymes cut poorly at the very end of a linear fragment. The site has to sit a few bases in. So stuffer bases go outside it. Every supplier publishes a table for this. It is called cleavage close to the end of D N A fragments. It gives how many bases each enzyme needs. Leaving them out gives a design that looks correct on paper. It then fails at the bench. The P C R product is simply not cut. And the ligation has nothing to work with.”',
    ezcn:'因为<b>限制酶在线性片段的最末端切不动</b>。<b>位点必须往里挪几个碱基，外面留填充碱基</b>。<b>每家供应商都发表一张表叫「靠近 DNA 片段末端的切割」</b>，<b>写明每个酶需要几个碱基</b>。<b>不留的话，设计在纸上看着对，到台子上就废了</b>：<b>PCR 产物根本没被切开，连接反应没东西可连。</b>',
 en:'“Because restriction enzymes cut poorly at the very end of a linear DNA fragment. The site has to sit a few bases in, so stuffer bases go outside it. Every supplier publishes a table called cleavage close to the end of DNA fragments giving how many bases each enzyme needs. Leaving them out gives a design that looks correct on paper and fails at the bench, because the PCR product simply is not cut and the ligation has nothing to work with.”',
 cn:'<b>「纸上对、台面上失败」是这一组的共同形状。</b><span class="pg">L2 s.15</span><br><b>这条也是酶切失败排查清单的第二项</b>：甲基化 → 离末端太近 → 缓冲液和星号活性。'},
{r:'高', q:'Your Golden Gate assembly gives truncated products. What did you forget?',
    ez:'“Domestication. A part may still contain an internal site for the assembly enzyme. That site is cut during the reaction. So the part is fragmented. The pieces then assemble into truncated products. You remove internal sites beforehand with silent mutations. It is a one time cost per part. That is exactly why standardised part collections exist. MoClo and GoldenBraid are examples. Once a part is domesticated it is reusable for ever.”',
    ezcn:'<b>忘了「驯化」domestication。</b><b>某个零件里如果还留着组装酶的内部识别位点，反应过程中它会被切开</b>，<b>零件碎掉，碎片再组装成截短的产物</b>。<b>做法是事先用同义突变把内部位点去掉</b>——<b>每个零件只需要付一次这个代价</b>。<b>MoClo、GoldenBraid 这些标准化零件库存在的理由就在这儿：驯化过一次，永远可以复用。</b>',
 en:'“Domestication. If a part still contains an internal site for the assembly enzyme, that site is cut during the reaction, so the part is fragmented and the pieces assemble into truncated products. You remove internal sites beforehand with silent mutations. It is a one time cost per part, and it is exactly why standardised part collections such as MoClo and GoldenBraid exist, because once a part is domesticated it is reusable for ever.”',
 cn:'<b>这条问出来的概率不低</b>，因为它是 Golden Gate 唯一写出来的缺点。<span class="pg">L2 s.20–21</span><br>⚠ 顺势可以给第二个坑：<b>256 是理论上限</b>，回文末端会自连、差一个碱基的末端会错连，所以末端组合要用工具挑。（两条都在 beyondPoints。）'},
{r:'中', q:'You ordered the reverse primer exactly as you wrote it out. What happens?',
 en:'“It binds nothing. A reverse primer is normally written out in the sense orientation so the logic is readable, with the gene end, the spacer, the site and the stuffer in order. But the real primer has to anneal to the top strand, so it must be synthesised as the reverse complement of what was written. Copying the sense strand onto an order form gives an oligonucleotide that anneals nowhere, and it is the easiest mark on a design question to throw away.”',
 cn:'<b>幻灯片自己用这句话结束那道练习。</b><span class="pg">L2 s.35–43</span><br><b>这条值得背，因为它零机制、纯粹是丢不起的那一分。</b>（在 beyondPoints。）'},
{r:'中', q:'You transformed and got thousands of colonies, but none of them has the insert. What is the most likely cause?',
 en:'“Self ligated empty vector. A vector cut with one enzyme, or with two enzymes that happen to leave compatible ends, has two complementary ends and can close on itself, and empty circular vector transforms extremely efficiently. So the plate is full and none of it is what I wanted. There are two fixes. A directional double digest with incompatible ends makes self ligation impossible. Dephosphorylating the vector removes the five prime phosphates that the ligase needs.”',
 cn:'<b>先说现象为什么是「菌落很多」而不是「菌落很少」</b>——空载体转化效率高，这正是它成为最大背景来源的原因。<span class="pg">L2 s.15</span><br><b>两个解法里定向双酶切是更好的那个</b>，因为它顺带把方向也定死了。'}
]},

{g:'他要数字怎么办', gn:'这张卡上的数几乎全在幻灯片里，<b>可以放心报</b>。但报完要立刻给判据。<b>编一个不存在的数是这场考试里最危险的动作</b>（LOGIC 第 11 条）。', items:[
{r:'高', q:'How many fragments can Golden Gate assemble at once?',
    ez:'“The reaction takes a plasmid plus up to ten inserts in one tube. Efficiency above ninety per cent is routine for five to ten fragments. A four base overhang gives two hundred and fifty six possible sequences. But that is a theoretical maximum. It is not a working number. Palindromic overhangs self ligate. And overhangs differing by one base mis ligate. With a high fidelity set chosen by a design tool, more than twenty fragments is achievable.”',
    ezcn:'<b>一管里可以放一个质粒 ＋ 最多十个插入片段</b>，<b>五到十个片段做到 90% 以上效率是常规</b>。<b>四碱基末端理论上有 256 种</b>，<b>但那是理论上限不是工作数字</b>：<b>回文末端会自连，差一个碱基的末端会错连</b>。<b>用设计工具挑一套高保真末端，二十个以上片段也做得到。</b>',
 en:'“The reaction takes a plasmid plus up to ten inserts in one tube, and efficiency above ninety per cent is routine for five to ten fragments. The four base overhang gives two hundred and fifty six possible sequences, but that is a theoretical maximum rather than a working number, because palindromic overhangs self ligate and overhangs differing by one base mis ligate. With a high fidelity set chosen by a design tool, more than twenty fragments is achievable.”',
 cn:'<b>这条演示了「报数之后立刻给判据」</b>：256 是真的，但它不是能同时用的数。<span class="pg">L2 s.20–21</span><br>⚠ <b>上限十个插入片段和 90% 在幻灯片上；保真度矩阵和「二十个以上」在 beyondPoints</b>，引的是 NEB 的 Potapov 等人 2018 年那篇。'},
{r:'高', q:'How long are the overlaps, and how long are the overhangs?',
    ez:'“L I C gives a single stranded overhang of about fifteen bases. Its tails are twelve to eighteen. Gibson uses designed overlaps of twenty to forty base pairs. NEBuilder HiFi tolerates shorter ones, around sixteen to twenty. A type two S enzyme leaves four bases. A restriction enzyme sticky end is also about four. A fifteen base anneal is stable on its own. So no ligase is needed there. A four base anneal is not stable on its own.”',
    ezcn:'<b>LIC</b> 给出<b>约 15 个碱基的单链末端</b>（尾巴 12–18）。<b>Gibson</b> 用<b>设计好的 20–40 bp 重叠</b>（NEBuilder HiFi 能接受 16–20）。<b>Ⅱ-S 型酶留 4 个碱基</b>，<b>普通限制酶的粘性末端也是 4 个左右</b>。<b>15 个碱基的退火本身就稳，所以那里不需要连接酶；4 个碱基的退火不稳。</b>',
 en:'“LIC gives a single stranded overhang of about fifteen bases, from tails of twelve to eighteen. Gibson uses designed overlaps of twenty to forty base pairs, and NEBuilder HiFi tolerates shorter ones around sixteen to twenty. A type two S enzyme leaves four bases. A restriction enzyme sticky end is also about four. A fifteen base anneal is stable enough on its own that no ligase is needed. A four base anneal is not.”',
 cn:'<b>把四个数放在一起说</b>，比分开报有力得多：它一句话解释了为什么 LIC 和 Gibson 可以不用连接酶而酶切克隆不行。<span class="pg">L2 s.29–32</span><br>⚠ 「高好几个数量级」这个比较在 <b>beyondPoints</b>，说的时候别说成幻灯片的话。'},
{r:'中', q:'What are the copy numbers, and what are the plasmid sizes?',
 en:'“Plasmids run from about fifteen hundred to twenty thousand base pairs, and smaller is better. The vector pUC uses a mutated pMB1 origin and sits at five hundred to seven hundred copies. The vector pBluescript uses a mutated ColE1 with F1 and gives three hundred to five hundred. Both pET and pGEX use pBR322 and have only fifteen to twenty copies. The pattern is that cloning vectors are high copy because their only job is yield, and expression vectors are low copy because high copy number is a metabolic burden.”',
 cn:'<b>报完数立刻给那条模式</b>，否则这就是一张要背的表。<span class="pg">L2 s.4–6</span><br>⚠ <b>数字在幻灯片上，代谢负担的解释在 beyondPoints。</b>'},
{r:'中', q:'How long does a ligation take, and at what temperature?',
 en:'“T4 ligation is either overnight at sixteen degrees or ten minutes at room temperature, and optimised kits and engineered variants exist. Golden Gate cycles between about thirty seven degrees to cut and sixteen to ligate, for twenty to forty cycles. Gibson is isothermal at fifty degrees. TOPO TA takes five minutes at room temperature, because the energy is already stored in the enzyme DNA bond rather than having to come from ATP.”',
 cn:'<b>四个条件放在一起，正好按「谁提供能量、谁提供选择性」排开。</b><span class="pg">L2 s.15 · s.20–21 · s.26–28 · s.31–32</span><br>⚠ <b>他如果问「为什么是 16 °C 不是 4 °C」，那已经没有数了</b>，给判据：<b>低温让退火的末端待得住，同时酶还有足够的活性</b>，具体值按试剂盒。别编。'},
{r:'中', q:'How efficient is Gateway, and how big is the scar?',
 en:'“Above ninety five per cent positive clones, and the scar is about eight amino acids. Those two numbers belong together, because the same design produces both. The att sites are what the recombinase reads, so they have to remain in the product, and since they sit at the fusion junction they are translated. The efficiency and the scar are one design decision rather than two facts.”',
 cn:'<b>「同一个设计既给了效率也给了疤」这句话是这条答案的重点。</b><span class="pg">L2 s.22–25</span><br>att 位点的长度也要能报：<b>attB 25 · attP 243 · attL 100 · attR 168 nt</b>。'}
]},

{g:'为什么类', gn:'这一族的「为什么」大多落在同一处：<b>末端的来处决定了其余全部性质</b>。再往下就是热力学。', items:[
{r:'高', q:'Why is cutting outside the recognition site such a big deal?',
    ez:'“Because one fact produces both advantages of Golden Gate. The recognition site ends up on the small discarded piece. So it is absent from the product. That makes the junction scarless. It also makes a correct junction impossible to cut again. And the enzyme does not dictate the overhang sequence. So I design each four base junction myself. The assembly then becomes directional and specific. Scarless, one pot and multi fragment are not three properties. They are one property seen three times.”',
    ezcn:'因为<b>一个事实同时产出 Golden Gate 的两个好处</b>。<b>识别位点落在被扔掉的那一小块上，所以它不在产物里</b>——<b>这既让接缝无疤，也让接对了的接缝再也切不开</b>。<b>而且末端序列不由酶决定</b>，<b>四个碱基的接缝是我自己设计的</b>，<b>于是组装变成定向而且专一的</b>。<b>「无疤、一锅、多片段」不是三个性质，是同一个性质的三种说法。</b>',
 en:'“Because one fact produces both of Golden Gate advantages. The recognition site ends up on the small piece that is discarded, so it is absent from the product. That makes the junction scarless, and it also makes a correct junction impossible to cut again. And the enzyme does not dictate the overhang sequence, so I design each of the four base junctions myself and the assembly becomes directional and specific. Scarless, one pot and multi fragment are not three properties. They are one property seen three times.”',
 cn:'<b>「一个性质看三遍」这个说法值分</b>，因为它表明你不是在背优点清单。<span class="pg">L2 s.20–21</span>'},
{r:'高', q:'Why is Gateway not simply the best method, if it is the most efficient?',
    ez:'“Because efficiency is not the only axis. It costs money. It needs special cells to propagate the destination vector. And it leaves about eight amino acids in the final protein. For routine expression that is irrelevant. But some jobs are different. An authentic N terminus, a crystal structure, a signal peptide or a protease site. There those residues change the very thing being studied. So the right question is not which method is best. It is which constraint I am under.”',
    ezcn:'因为<b>效率不是唯一的轴</b>。<b>它贵</b>，<b>要专门的细胞来繁殖目的载体</b>，<b>而且在最终蛋白上留下大约八个氨基酸</b>。<b>常规表达无所谓</b>；<b>但要一个真实的 N 端、要做晶体结构、要信号肽、要蛋白酶切位点的时候，那几个残基改变的正是你在研究的那个东西</b>。<b>所以正确的问题不是「哪个方法最好」，是「我受的是哪个约束」——讲义也是这么答的。</b>',
 en:'“Because efficiency is not the only axis. It costs money, it needs special cells to propagate the destination vector, and it leaves about eight amino acids in the final protein. For routine expression that is irrelevant. For an authentic N terminus, a crystal structure, a signal peptide or a protease site, those residues change the very thing being studied. So the right question is not which method is best but which constraint I am under, and the lecture answers it that way too.”',
 cn:'<b>这条是回答「怎么选」那道题的缩小版</b>，形状一样：<b>先问约束，再选方法。</b><span class="pg">L2 s.22–25 · L2 s.33</span>'},
{r:'中', q:'Why does tracking the phosphates explain so much of a cloning protocol?',
 en:'“Because ligase has exactly one requirement, a five prime phosphate and a three prime hydroxyl, both present. Every end in a protocol either satisfies it or does not. Restriction ends carry a five prime phosphate, so they ligate directly. Synthetic oligonucleotide ends carry a hydroxyl, so a PCR product cannot ligate at that end. And removing the phosphates from a vector is how you stop it closing on itself. Three unrelated looking steps come from one rule.”',
 cn:'<b>这条是这张卡最省力的杠杆</b>，值得主动说出来。<span class="pg">L1 s.28</span><br>补救的两条也要跟着：<b>订磷酸化引物</b>，或者 <b>T4 PNK</b> 把 ATP 的磷酸转上去。<b>反应类型接卡 x-rxn。</b>'},
{r:'中', q:'Why is it a legitimate answer to say you use whatever your lab already runs?',
 en:'“Because the constraints are practical and not only technical. The technical rule gives a shortlist, but a method only works well when the protocols are optimised, the reagents are on the shelf and the standard vectors already exist. That is why the lecture answers the question that way. It is also why large centres run core facilities doing cloning at high throughput. That saves cost and it frees you for the non trivial work.”',
 cn:'<b>这是幻灯片自己的答案，不是一句托词。</b><span class="pg">L2 s.33</span><br>⚠ <b>但顺序不能反</b>：先给技术上的决策规则，再给这一句。只给这一句会听起来像不知道方法。'},
{r:'中', q:'Why is a library a harder cloning problem than a single construct?',
 en:'“Because a library is not one clone, it is very many, so the efficiency of the joining step stops being a convenience and becomes the size of the library itself. Everything that is merely annoying for one construct becomes limiting here. The junction has to be scarless so every member is in frame with the anchor and the tags. The parts are reused every round, so a one pot method earns back its setup cost. And the transformation has to be electroporation, because the number of successful events is already small.”',
 cn:'<b>这是这张卡的段 4，也是她的主场</b>：文库、选择、fitness landscape 接卡 <b>land</b>，电穿孔接卡 <b>14</b>，质粒进去之后接卡 <b>pe-expr</b>。<br>⚠ <b>不要给文库大小的数字</b>，笔记里没有。要数就给判据：<b>成功事件本来就少的时候，效率才要紧。</b>'}
]}
]
});
